 2025"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "california", "eyebrow": "Another line", "title": "California drew its line at 10^26", "body": "SB 53, signed on September 29, 2025, covers models above 10^26 operations. Firms with over $500 million in revenue must publish a safety framework.", "bullets": ["Compute spent on fine-tuning counts toward the line.", "Penalties reach $1 million per violation."], "sources": [{"url": "https://fpf.org/blog/californias-sb-53-the-first-frontier-ai-law-explained/", "label": "Future of Privacy Forum, California's SB 53 explained"}]}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "Which lines does each training run cross?", "buckets": ["Below 10^25", "EU line only", "Above 10^26 too"], "items": [{"text": "GPT-3: 3.14 × 10^23", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "A run at 5 × 10^24", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Llama 3 405B: 3.8 × 10^25", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "A run at 9 × 10^25", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "A run at 2 × 10^26", "bucket": 2}], "explanation": "The EU line sits at 10^25 and California's at 10^26. Llama 3's flagship crossed the first one."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "An EU provider learns its model will cross 10^25. What must it do within two weeks?", "options": ["Publish its model weights", "Stop selling in the EU", "Notify the European Commission"], "correctIndex": 2, "explanation": "It must notify the Commission without delay, within two weeks at the latest. It can argue its model poses no systemic risk."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "You run a California lab with $600 million in revenue. Your next model will take 2 × 10^26 operations.", "prompt": "What does SB 53 ask of you?", "options": ["Publish a framework and a transparency report", "Get a state license before training", "Nothing, since only the EU has such rules"], "consequences": ["That matches what the law asks of large frontier developers.", "SB 53 sets disclosure duties, not a training license.", "California set its own line at 10^26."], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Large frontier developers publish a safety framework, and a transparency report before deploying a frontier model."}, {"id": "lens-invest", "kind": "info", "title": "Compliance scales with compute", "body": "Over 30 models had crossed the EU line by June 2025. Each brings testing and reporting duties into its maker's costs.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/data-insights/models-over-1e25-flop", "label": "Epoch AI, models over 10^25 FLOP, Jun 2025"}, {"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for GPAI providers"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI rules, training compute is the trigger regulators can measure.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu/en/ai-act/article-51", "label": "EU AI Act Service Desk, Article 51"}, {"url": "https://fpf.org/blog/californias-sb-53-the-first-frontier-ai-law-explained/", "label": "Future of Privacy Forum, California's SB 53 explained"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "The EU presumes systemic risk above 10^25 training operations, and California set its line at 10^26. Over 30 models had crossed the EU line by June 2025.", "sectionKey": "risk"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$3cab161e-6a08-5cd6-816b-91bf65cc1efe$ml$::uuid, $ml$ai$ml$, $ml$Laws that count operations$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-35$ml$, $ml$month-2$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:build_startup$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "ai-d35-build_startup", "title": "Laws that count operations", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "A compute number now triggers legal duties.", "eyebrow": "Day 35 · The rules", "headline": "In the EU, a model trained with more than 10^25 operations is presumed to carry systemic risk.", "fullText": "Article 51 of the AI Act ties extra duties to training compute. Since August 2, 2025, a provider whose model crosses that line must notify the European Commission within two weeks. It must then run evaluations with adversarial testing, report serious incidents and protect the model with adequate cybersecurity.", "sources": [{"url": "https://ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu/en/ai-act/article-51", "label": "EU AI Act Service Desk, Article 51"}, {"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for GPAI providers"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "proxy", "eyebrow": "Why compute", "text": "The law presumes high-impact capabilities from training compute alone.", "highlight": "The Commission can move the line as algorithms and hardware improve.", "sources": [{"url": "https://ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu/en/ai-act/article-51", "label": "EU AI Act Service Desk, Article 51"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "count", "eyebrow": "How many", "text": "GPT-4, released in March 2023, was the first model trained at that scale.", "highlight": "By June 2025, Epoch AI counted over 30 models from 12 developers above it.", "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/data-insights/models-over-1e25-flop", "label": "Epoch AI, models over 10^25 FLOP, Jun 2025"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "california", "eyebrow": "Another line", "title": "California drew its line at 10^26", "body": "SB 53, signed on September 29, 2025, covers models above 10^26 operations. Firms with over $500 million in revenue must publish a safety framework.", "bullets": ["Compute spent on fine-tuning counts toward the line.", "Penalties reach $1 million per violation."], "sources": [{"url": "https://fpf.org/blog/californias-sb-53-the-first-frontier-ai-law-explained/", "label": "Future of Privacy Forum, California's SB 53 explained"}]}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "Which lines does each training run cross?", "buckets": ["Below 10^25", "EU line only", "Above 10^26 too"], "items": [{"text": "GPT-3: 3.14 × 10^23", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "A run at 5 × 10^24", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Llama 3 405B: 3.8 × 10^25", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "A run at 9 × 10^25", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "A run at 2 × 10^26", "bucket": 2}], "explanation": "The EU line sits at 10^25 and California's at 10^26. Llama 3's flagship crossed the first one."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "An EU provider learns its model will cross 10^25. What must it do within two weeks?", "options": ["Publish its model weights", "Stop selling in the EU", "Notify the European Commission"], "correctIndex": 2, "explanation": "It must notify the Commission without delay, within two weeks at the latest. It can argue its model poses no systemic risk."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "You run a California lab with $600 million in revenue. Your next model will take 2 × 10^26 operations.", "prompt": "What does SB 53 ask of you?", "options": ["Publish a framework and a transparency report", "Get a state license before training", "Nothing, since only the EU has such rules"], "consequences": ["That matches what the law asks of large frontier developers.", "SB 53 sets disclosure duties, not a training license.", "California set its own line at 10^26."], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Large frontier developers publish a safety framework, and a transparency report before deploying a frontier model."}, {"id": "lens-build_startup", "kind": "info", "title": "Most startups sit below the line", "body": "Fine-tuning an existing model rarely adds enough compute to cross 10^25. Know where your model sits before you worry.", "eyebrow": "For founders", "sources": [{"url": "https://ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu/en/ai-act/article-51", "label": "EU AI Act Service Desk, Article 51"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI rules, training compute is the trigger regulators can measure.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu/en/ai-act/article-51", "label": "EU AI Act Service Desk, Article 51"}, {"url": "https://fpf.org/blog/californias-sb-53-the-first-frontier-ai-law-explained/", "label": "Future of Privacy Forum, California's SB 53 explained"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "The EU presumes systemic risk above 10^25 training operations, and California set its line at 10^26. Over 30 models had crossed the EU line by June 2025.", "sectionKey": "incumbents"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
