 "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Large frontier developers publish a safety framework, and a transparency report before deploying a frontier model."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "A law with an exponent", "body": "The EU wrote a number with 25 zeros into law. Above it, a model is presumed to carry systemic risk.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu/en/ai-act/article-51", "label": "EU AI Act Service Desk, Article 51"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI rules, training compute is the trigger regulators can measure.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu/en/ai-act/article-51", "label": "EU AI Act Service Desk, Article 51"}, {"url": "https://fpf.org/blog/californias-sb-53-the-first-frontier-ai-law-explained/", "label": "Future of Privacy Forum, California's SB 53 explained"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "The EU presumes systemic risk above 10^25 training operations, and California set its line at 10^26. Over 30 models had crossed the EU line by June 2025.", "sectionKey": "rules"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$925c6b1f-7aaf-584f-94e9-61a5856a935c$ml$::uuid, $ml$ai$ml$, $ml$When bigger stopped being enough$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-36$ml$, $ml$month-2$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "ai-d36-career", "title": "When bigger stopped being enough", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "The biggest GPT did not stay long.", "eyebrow": "Day 36 · Where it breaks", "headline": "In February 2025, OpenAI launched GPT-4.5, its largest model, at $75 per million input tokens.", "fullText": "That was 30 times GPT-4o's $2.50. GPT-4.5 scaled up pre-training, the recipe behind every earlier GPT, yet trailed reasoning models on hard math and science tests. In April 2025, OpenAI said it would pull GPT-4.5 from its API by July 14, because GPT-4.1 matched or beat it in key areas for much less.", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/27/openai-unveils-gpt-4-5-orion-its-largest-ai-model-yet", "label": "TechCrunch, OpenAI unveils GPT-4.5, Feb 2025"}, {"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/04/14/openai-plans-to-wind-down-gpt-4-5-its-largest-ever-ai-model-in-its-api", "label": "TechCrunch, OpenAI to wind down GPT-4.5 in its API, Apr 2025"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "peak", "eyebrow": "The warning", "text": "In December 2024, Ilya Sutskever said: \"we've achieved peak data.\"", "highlight": "He said pre-training as we know it will unquestionably end.", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/27/openai-unveils-gpt-4-5-orion-its-largest-ai-model-yet", "label": "TechCrunch, OpenAI unveils GPT-4.5, Feb 2025"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "think", "eyebrow": "A new axis", "text": "OpenAI found its o1 model improves with more training and with more time to think before answering.", "highlight": "On the 2024 AIME math exam, o1 scored 74% and GPT-4o 12%.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Test-time compute", "definition": "Compute a model spends while answering, such as thinking through steps first."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://openai.com/index/learning-to-reason-with-llms/", "label": "OpenAI, Learning to reason with LLMs, Sep 2024"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "limits", "eyebrow": "Open question", "title": "New curve, new limits", "body": "OpenAI says the limits on scaling this approach differ a lot from those of pre-training. It is still studying them.", "sources": [{"url": "https://openai.com/index/learning-to-reason-with-llms/", "label": "OpenAI, Learning to reason with LLMs, Sep 2024"}]}, {"kind": "spotFake", "id": "fake", "prompt": "One of these is false. Tap it.", "statements": ["GPT-4.5 cost $75 per million input tokens in the API.", "o1 scored 74% on the 2024 AIME with one try per problem.", "OpenAI kept GPT-4.5 as its API flagship through 2025."], "fakeIndex": 2, "explanation": "OpenAI said in April 2025 that GPT-4.5 would leave the API by July 14."}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-aime", "prompt": "On the 2024 AIME, o1 scored 74%. What percent did GPT-4o score?", "min": 0, "max": 60, "value": 12, "unit": "%", "explanation": "GPT-4o averaged 12%. Thinking longer before answering made the difference."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "Your product must solve hard multi-step math problems on a fixed budget.", "prompt": "Which kind of model do you test first?", "options": ["A reasoning model that thinks before answering", "The largest pre-trained model you can buy", "The smallest model, answering instantly"], "consequences": ["o1 beat GPT-4o on AIME, 74% to 12%, by thinking longer.", "GPT-4.5 was the largest and still trailed reasoning models on math.", "Instant answers are cheap but weak on multi-step problems."], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "For hard reasoning, spending compute at answer time can beat spending it on size."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Have a view on the next curve", "body": "Pre-training gains look harder to get, and thinking time is a new lever. Say which one you would bet on, and why.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/27/openai-unveils-gpt-4-5-orion-its-largest-ai-model-yet", "label": "TechCrunch, OpenAI unveils GPT-4.5, Feb 2025"}, {"url": "https://openai.com/index/learning-to-reason-with-llms/", "label": "OpenAI, Learning to reason with LLMs, Sep 2024"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI, when bigger stops paying, labs scale thinking time instead.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/27/openai-unveils-gpt-4-5-orion-its-largest-ai-model-yet", "label": "TechCrunch, OpenAI unveils GPT-4.5, Feb 2025"}, {"url": "https://openai.com/index/learning-to-reason-with-llms/", "label": "OpenAI, Learning to reason with LLMs, Sep 2024"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "GPT-4.5 was OpenAI's largest model, cost 30 times GPT-4o per input token and left the API within months. Labs now scale thinking time, as o1 did when it jumped to 74% on AIME.", "sectionKey": "my_view"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
