cost 30 times GPT-4o per input token and left the API within months. Serving cost can sink a bigger model.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/27/openai-unveils-gpt-4-5-orion-its-largest-ai-model-yet", "label": "TechCrunch, OpenAI unveils GPT-4.5, Feb 2025"}, {"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/04/14/openai-plans-to-wind-down-gpt-4-5-its-largest-ever-ai-model-in-its-api", "label": "TechCrunch, OpenAI to wind down GPT-4.5 in its API, Apr 2025"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI, when bigger stops paying, labs scale thinking time instead.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/27/openai-unveils-gpt-4-5-orion-its-largest-ai-model-yet", "label": "TechCrunch, OpenAI unveils GPT-4.5, Feb 2025"}, {"url": "https://openai.com/index/learning-to-reason-with-llms/", "label": "OpenAI, Learning to reason with LLMs, Sep 2024"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "GPT-4.5 was OpenAI's largest model, cost 30 times GPT-4o per input token and left the API within months. Labs now scale thinking time, as o1 did when it jumped to 74% on AIME.", "sectionKey": "review"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
