 scored 74% on a hard math exam where GPT-4o scored 12%. It got there by thinking longer, not by being bigger.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://openai.com/index/learning-to-reason-with-llms/", "label": "OpenAI, Learning to reason with LLMs, Sep 2024"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI, when bigger stops paying, labs scale thinking time instead.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/27/openai-unveils-gpt-4-5-orion-its-largest-ai-model-yet", "label": "TechCrunch, OpenAI unveils GPT-4.5, Feb 2025"}, {"url": "https://openai.com/index/learning-to-reason-with-llms/", "label": "OpenAI, Learning to reason with LLMs, Sep 2024"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "GPT-4.5 was OpenAI's largest model, cost 30 times GPT-4o per input token and left the API within months. Labs now scale thinking time, as o1 did when it jumped to 74% on AIME.", "sectionKey": "frontier"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b459968b-7fc3-5afc-bdc2-c6f044d3cbdd$ml$::uuid, $ml$ai$ml$, $ml$The final run is a fraction of the bill$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-37$ml$, $ml$month-2$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "ai-d37-career", "title": "The final run is a fraction of the bill", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "The famous number is only the last step.", "eyebrow": "Day 37 · Training costs", "headline": "In 2024, OpenAI spent about $5 billion on R&D compute. Only about $500 million went to final training runs.", "fullText": "A final training run is the one that produces a released model. Epoch AI estimated that such runs took roughly 10% of OpenAI's 2024 R&D compute spending. The rest went to scaling experiments, synthetic data, basic research and other R&D. So the headline cost of training a model is only a slice of what building it costs.", "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/gradient-updates/r-and-d-vs-training-compute", "label": "Epoch AI, Final training runs account for a minority of R&D compute spending, Mar 2026"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "tests", "eyebrow": "The hidden runs", "text": "Most research compute goes to runs that never become a product.", "highlight": "Final runs took 22.6% of MiniMax's R&D compute and 12.3% of Z.ai's.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Final training run", "definition": "The run that produces the model a company actually releases."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/gradient-updates/r-and-d-vs-training-compute", "label": "Epoch AI, Final training runs account for a minority of R&D compute spending, Mar 2026"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "people", "eyebrow": "The people", "text": "Compute is not the whole bill. People are a large share too.", "highlight": "R&D staff made up 29% to 49% of development cost in Epoch's study.", "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/publications/how-much-does-it-cost-to-train-frontier-ai-models", "label": "Epoch AI, How much does it cost to train frontier AI models?, Jun 2024"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "shares", "eyebrow": "The full bill", "title": "Chips first, people second, power last", "body": "Across four models including GPT-4 and Gemini Ultra, hardware was 47% to 67% of development cost. Energy was only 2% to 6%.", "bullets": ["Epoch's headline costs count hardware and energy for the final run only."], "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/publications/how-much-does-it-cost-to-train-frontier-ai-models", "label": "Epoch AI, How much does it cost to train frontier AI models?, Jun 2024"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-final", "prompt": "OpenAI spent about $5 billion on R&D compute in 2024. About how many millions went to final training runs?", "min": 0, "max": 2000, "value": 500, "unit": "M", "explanation": "About $500 million, roughly 10%. The rest went to experiments, synthetic data and basic research."}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "Is it in the headline training cost, or only in the full bill?", "buckets": ["Headline cost", "Only the full bill"], "items": [{"text": "GPUs for the run that ships", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Energy for that final run", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Hundreds of test runs", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "Researcher salaries and equity", "bucket": 1}], "explanation": "Headline estimates count hardware and energy for the final run. Experiments and staff only show up in the full development cost."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "A startup says it trained its model for $3 million. It wants your money to build the next one.", "prompt": "What do you ask first?", "options": ["Which cloud provider it trained on", "What its research and test runs cost", "How many people use the model today"], "consequences": ["The provider matters less than the full bill.", "The final run can be a small slice of total R&D compute.", "Usage says nothing about what training cost."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "At OpenAI, final runs were about 10% of R&D compute. Ask for the whole bill, not the last run."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Separate the run from the program", "body": "When someone quotes a training cost, ask if it covers only the final run. At OpenAI that was about 10% of R&D compute.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/gradient-updates/r-and-d-vs-training-compute", "label": "Epoch AI, Final training runs account for a minority of R&D compute spending, Mar 2026"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI, the final training run is only a slice of what a model costs.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/gradient-updates/r-and-d-vs-training-compute", "label": "Epoch AI, Final training runs account for a minority of R&D compute spending, Mar 2026"}, {"url": "https://epoch.ai/publications/how-much-does-it-cost-to-train-frontier-ai-models", "label": "Epoch AI, How much does it cost to train frontier AI models?, Jun 2024"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "OpenAI spent about $5 billion on R&D compute in 2024 and only about $500 million on final training runs. Staff and experiments make the full bill much bigger than the headline.", "sectionKey": "players"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
