Fake", "id": "fake", "prompt": "One of these is false. Tap it.", "statements": ["NVIDIA pledged up to $10 billion to Anthropic.", "OpenAI committed to buy $250 billion of Azure services.", "Anthropic agreed to run only on Microsoft hardware."], "fakeIndex": 2, "explanation": "Anthropic's compute spans AWS Trainium, Google TPUs and NVIDIA GPUs."}, {"id": "lens-invest", "kind": "info", "title": "Discount circular revenue", "body": "When a supplier's investment comes back as its own sales, ask how much of that demand would exist without the investment.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.anthropic.com/news/microsoft-nvidia-anthropic-announce-strategic-partnerships", "label": "Anthropic, Microsoft, NVIDIA and Anthropic announce strategic partnerships, Nov 2025"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI, whoever sells the compute increasingly owns a piece of whoever buys it.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.anthropic.com/news/microsoft-nvidia-anthropic-announce-strategic-partnerships", "label": "Anthropic, Microsoft, NVIDIA and Anthropic announce strategic partnerships, Nov 2025"}, {"url": "https://www.scmp.com/tech/big-tech/article/3330714/microsoft-holds-27-openai-revamped-partnership", "label": "SCMP, Microsoft holds 27% of OpenAI in revamped partnership, Oct 2025"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Microsoft and NVIDIA pledged up to $15 billion to Anthropic, which pledged $30 billion back to Azure. Compute sellers now own stakes in their biggest buyers.", "sectionKey": "thesis"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
