 rental estimates come out about twice as high as owned hardware.", "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/publications/how-much-does-it-cost-to-train-frontier-ai-models", "label": "Epoch AI, How much does it cost to train frontier AI models?, Jun 2024"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "billion", "eyebrow": "The next milestone", "title": "Runs over $1 billion by 2027", "body": "If the trend holds, Epoch expects the largest runs to cost more than $1 billion by 2027. That would keep the frontier to the best-funded labs.", "bullets": ["GPU compute per dollar doubles about every 2.1 years."], "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/publications/how-much-does-it-cost-to-train-frontier-ai-models", "label": "Epoch AI, How much does it cost to train frontier AI models?, Jun 2024"}, {"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.21015", "label": "Cottier et al., The rising costs of training frontier AI models, 2024"}, {"url": "https://epoch.ai/publications/trends-in-machine-learning-hardware", "label": "Epoch AI, Trends in machine learning hardware, Nov 2023"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-growth", "prompt": "If the biggest run costs 2.4 times more each year, about how many times more does it cost after three years?", "min": 0, "max": 40, "value": 14, "unit": "x", "explanation": "2.4 × 2.4 × 2.4 is about 13.8. At that pace a $490 million run becomes several billion."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "What does Epoch's $490 million estimate for Grok 4 leave out?", "options": ["Staff, experiments and serving users", "The GPUs used in the final run", "The electricity for the final run"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "It counts the final run only. Staff, experiments and serving can add a lot."}, {"kind": "faceOff", "id": "face", "prompt": "Same training run, two ways to count. Which estimate comes out higher?", "left": {"name": "Owned hardware", "note": "Chip cost spread over its life, plus energy"}, "right": {"name": "Cloud rental", "note": "Hourly prices paid to a cloud"}, "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Epoch found cloud estimates about twice as high on average."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "A town's worth of power", "body": "Training Grok 4 used about 310 gigawatt-hours, enough to power a town of 4,000 Americans, by Epoch's estimate.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/data-insights/grok-4-training-resources", "label": "Epoch AI, Grok 4 training resources, Sep 2025"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI, the bill for the biggest training run multiplies every year.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/publications/how-much-does-it-cost-to-train-frontier-ai-models", "label": "Epoch AI, How much does it cost to train frontier AI models?, Jun 2024"}, {"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.21015", "label": "Cottier et al., The rising costs of training frontier AI models, 2024"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Epoch put Grok 4's training at about $490 million. Frontier run costs grow about 2.4 times a year, and Epoch expects them to pass $1 billion by 2027 if that holds.", "sectionKey": "numbers"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$8d21286d-c4fd-5bdf-8db1-145b474fb58f$ml$::uuid, $ml$ai$ml$, $ml$A law that counts operations$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-41$ml$, $ml$month-2$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "ai-d41-career", "title": "A law that counts operations", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "Past a compute line, the paperwork starts.", "eyebrow": "Day 41 · The rules", "headline": "Since January 1, 2026, California's SB 53 has applied to AI models trained with more than 10^26 operations.", "fullText": "Governor Newsom signed the Transparency in Frontier Artificial Intelligence Act on September 29, 2025. The count includes the original run plus later fine-tuning and reinforcement learning. Developers must publish a transparency report before deploying a new frontier model and report critical safety incidents within 15 days. Penalties reach $1 million.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "big", "eyebrow": "The big developers", "text": "Some duties apply only to developers with more than $500 million in revenue.", "highlight": "They must publish a framework for how they manage catastrophic risk.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "eu", "eyebrow": "The EU line", "text": "The EU draws its line ten times lower, at 10^25 operations.", "highlight": "Above it, a model is presumed to carry systemic risk.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Systemic risk", "definition": "EU label for models presumed to match the most advanced, with extra duties."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "crowd", "eyebrow": "Who is above the line", "title": "Over 30 models had crossed 10^25", "body": "By June 2025, over 30 announced models from 12 developers had passed 10^25. GPT-4 was the first, in March 2023.", "bullets": ["Training at that scale costs tens of millions of dollars."], "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/data-insights/models-over-1e25-flop", "label": "Epoch AI, Models over 10^25 FLOP"}]}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "California or the EU?", "buckets": ["California SB 53", "EU AI Act"], "items": [{"text": "Line at 10^26 operations", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Line at 10^25 operations", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "Incident reports within 15 days", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Notify the Commission within two weeks", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "Extra duties above $500 million revenue", "bucket": 0}], "explanation": "California starts at 10^26 with a revenue test for big developers. The EU starts at 10^25 and wants notice within two weeks."}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-count", "prompt": "By June 2025, over how many announced models had crossed 10^25 operations?", "min": 0, "max": 100, "value": 30, "unit": "models", "explanation": "Over 30, from 12 developers, about two a month during 2024."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "Your lab's next model will pass 10^25 operations of training. You plan to offer it in the EU.", "prompt": "What do you do?", "options": ["Wait until the model launches", "Notify the Commission within two weeks", "Split training so no run crosses"], "consequences": ["The duty starts when you cross the line, not at launch.", "The EU wants notice within two weeks of crossing or knowing you will.", "The EU counts cumulative compute, so splitting does not help."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "The EU presumes systemic risk above 10^25 and requires notice within two weeks."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Know both compute lines", "body": "California starts at 10^26 operations, the EU at 10^25. Policy and safety teams track where each new model lands.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}, {"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI, the more compute a model takes, the more rules it has to meet.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}, {"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "California's SB 53 covers models trained with more than 10^26 operations, and the EU presumes systemic risk above 10^25. Compute is now a legal line.", "sectionKey": "risk"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
