g you will.", "The EU counts cumulative compute, so splitting does not help."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "The EU presumes systemic risk above 10^25 and requires notice within two weeks."}, {"id": "lens-invest", "kind": "info", "title": "Compliance scales with compute", "body": "Labs above 10^26 and $500 million in revenue carry the heaviest California duties, with penalties up to $1 million.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI, the more compute a model takes, the more rules it has to meet.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}, {"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "California's SB 53 covers models trained with more than 10^26 operations, and the EU presumes systemic risk above 10^25. Compute is now a legal line.", "sectionKey": "risk"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$aa725000-e464-56f6-b0ce-c68a3aaf044f$ml$::uuid, $ml$ai$ml$, $ml$A law that counts operations$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-41$ml$, $ml$month-2$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:build_startup$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "ai-d41-build_startup", "title": "A law that counts operations", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "Past a compute line, the paperwork starts.", "eyebrow": "Day 41 · The rules", "headline": "Since January 1, 2026, California's SB 53 has applied to AI models trained with more than 10^26 operations.", "fullText": "Governor Newsom signed the Transparency in Frontier Artificial Intelligence Act on September 29, 2025. The count includes the original run plus later fine-tuning and reinforcement learning. Developers must publish a transparency report before deploying a new frontier model and report critical safety incidents within 15 days. Penalties reach $1 million.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "big", "eyebrow": "The big developers", "text": "Some duties apply only to developers with more than $500 million in revenue.", "highlight": "They must publish a framework for how they manage catastrophic risk.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "eu", "eyebrow": "The EU line", "text": "The EU draws its line ten times lower, at 10^25 operations.", "highlight": "Above it, a model is presumed to carry systemic risk.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Systemic risk", "definition": "EU label for models presumed to match the most advanced, with extra duties."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "crowd", "eyebrow": "Who is above the line", "title": "Over 30 models had crossed 10^25", "body": "By June 2025, over 30 announced models from 12 developers had passed 10^25. GPT-4 was the first, in March 2023.", "bullets": ["Training at that scale costs tens of millions of dollars."], "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/data-insights/models-over-1e25-flop", "label": "Epoch AI, Models over 10^25 FLOP"}]}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "California or the EU?", "buckets": ["California SB 53", "EU AI Act"], "items": [{"text": "Line at 10^26 operations", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Line at 10^25 operations", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "Incident reports within 15 days", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Notify the Commission within two weeks", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "Extra duties above $500 million revenue", "bucket": 0}], "explanation": "California starts at 10^26 with a revenue test for big developers. The EU starts at 10^25 and wants notice within two weeks."}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-count", "prompt": "By June 2025, over how many announced models had crossed 10^25 operations?", "min": 0, "max": 100, "value": 30, "unit": "models", "explanation": "Over 30, from 12 developers, about two a month during 2024."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "Your lab's next model will pass 10^25 operations of training. You plan to offer it in the EU.", "prompt": "What do you do?", "options": ["Wait until the model launches", "Notify the Commission within two weeks", "Split training so no run crosses"], "consequences": ["The duty starts when you cross the line, not at launch.", "The EU wants notice within two weeks of crossing or knowing you will.", "The EU counts cumulative compute, so splitting does not help."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "The EU presumes systemic risk above 10^25 and requires notice within two weeks."}, {"id": "lens-build_startup", "kind": "info", "title": "Fine-tuners often sit below", "body": "Training at 10^25 costs tens of millions of dollars. In the EU, a fine-tuner becomes the provider only past a third of the original compute.", "eyebrow": "For founders", "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/data-insights/models-over-1e25-flop", "label": "Epoch AI, Models over 10^25 FLOP"}, {"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI, the more compute a model takes, the more rules it has to meet.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}, {"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "California's SB 53 covers models trained with more than 10^26 operations, and the EU presumes systemic risk above 10^25. Compute is now a legal line.", "sectionKey": "incumbents"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7c49b45b-94d8-581d-91ed-4322e80c5fc1$ml$::uuid, $ml$ai$ml$, $ml$A law that counts operations$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-41$ml$, $ml$month-2$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:curiosity$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "ai-d41-curiosity", "title": "A law that counts operations", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "Past a compute line, the paperwork starts.", "eyebrow": "Day 41 · The rules", "headline": "Since January 1, 2026, California's SB 53 has applied to AI models trained with more than 10^26 operations.", "fullText": "Governor Newsom signed the Transparency in Frontier Artificial Intelligence Act on September 29, 2025. The count includes the original run plus later fine-tuning and reinforcement learning. Developers must publish a transparency report before deploying a new frontier model and report critical safety incidents within 15 days. Penalties reach $1 million.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "big", "eyebrow": "The big developers", "text": "Some duties apply only to developers with more than $500 million in revenue.", "highlight": "They must publish a framework for how they manage catastrophic risk.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "eu", "eyebrow": "The EU line", "text": "The EU draws its line ten times lower, at 10^25 operations.", "highlight": "Above it, a model is presumed to carry systemic risk.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Systemic risk", "definition": "EU label for models presumed to match the most advanced, with extra duties."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "crowd", "eyebrow": "Who is above the line", "title": "Over 30 models had crossed 10^25", "body": "By June 2025, over 30 announced models from 12 developers had passed 10^25. GPT-4 was the first, in March 2023.", "bullets": ["Training at that scale costs tens of millions of dollars."], "sources": [{"url": "https://epoch.ai/data-insights/models-over-1e25-flop", "label": "Epoch AI, Models over 10^25 FLOP"}]}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "California or the EU?", "buckets": ["California SB 53", "EU AI Act"], "items": [{"text": "Line at 10^26 operations", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Line at 10^25 operations", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "Incident reports within 15 days", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Notify the Commission within two weeks", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "Extra duties above $500 million revenue", "bucket": 0}], "explanation": "California starts at 10^26 with a revenue test for big developers. The EU starts at 10^25 and wants notice within two weeks."}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-count", "prompt": "By June 2025, over how many announced models had crossed 10^25 operations?", "min": 0, "max": 100, "value": 30, "unit": "models", "explanation": "Over 30, from 12 developers, about two a month during 2024."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "Your lab's next model will pass 10^25 operations of training. You plan to offer it in the EU.", "prompt": "What do you do?", "options": ["Wait until the model launches", "Notify the Commission within two weeks", "Split training so no run crosses"], "consequences": ["The duty starts when you cross the line, not at launch.", "The EU wants notice within two weeks of crossing or knowing you will.", "The EU counts cumulative compute, so splitting does not help."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "The EU presumes systemic risk above 10^25 and requires notice within two weeks."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "Laws that count math", "body": "California and the EU now regulate AI partly by how many operations went into training it.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}, {"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI, the more compute a model takes, the more rules it has to meet.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}, {"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "California's SB 53 covers models trained with more than 10^26 operations, and the EU presumes systemic risk above 10^25. Compute is now a legal line.", "sectionKey": "rules"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$ef42e130-8c01-5c89-acc8-50bc231d6e9c$ml$::uuid, $ml$ai$ml$, $ml$A $278 billion bet on revenue$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-42$ml$, $ml$month-2$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "ai-d42-career", "title": "A $278 billion bet on revenue", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "The race runs on cash it has not earned yet.", "eyebrow": "Day 42 · Where it breaks", "headline": "In September 2026, OpenAI projected it would burn $278 billion in cash from 2026 to 2030.", "fullText": "The Financial Times reported the figures from a company presentation. OpenAI expects to spend about $856 billion on compute and infrastructure by the end of 2030, its largest cost. It forecasts revenue rising from $36 billion this year to $350 billion in 2030. It was on track to use up its March raise by 2028.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.thestar.com.my/tech/tech-news/2026/09/19/openai-forecasts-cash-burn-near-280-billion-by-2030-ft-reports", "label": "Reuters via The Star, OpenAI forecasts cash burn near $280 billion by 2030, Sep 2026"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "commit", "eyebrow": "The commitments", "text": "In November 2025, Sam Altman cited about $1.4 trillion of data center commitments over eight years.", "highlight": "OpenAI then expected above $20 billion of annualized revenue.", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/11/06/sam-altman-says-openai-has-20b-arr-and-about-1-4-trillion-in-data-center-commitments", "label": "TechCrunch, Altman cites $20B ARR and about $1.4 trillion of commitments, Nov 2025"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "warning", "eyebrow": "The warning", "text": "Central banks are watching the valuations behind the race.", "highlight": "In October 2025, the Bank of England said the risk of a sharp market correction had increased.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/financial-policy-committee-record/2025/october-2025", "label": "Bank of England, Financial Policy Committee record, Oct 2025"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "gap", "eyebrow": "The gap", "title": "Revenue has to grow tenfold", "body": "OpenAI's plan needs revenue to rise from $36 billion to $350 billion by 2030. Revenue would total about $840 billion, against $856 billion of compute.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.thestar.com.my/tech/tech-news/2026/09/19/openai-forecasts-cash-burn-near-280-billion-by-2030-ft-reports", "label": "Reuters via The Star, OpenAI forecasts cash burn near $280 billion by 2030, Sep 2026"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-x", "prompt": "From $36 billion this year to $350 billion in 2030: about how many times larger is that?", "min": 0, "max": 30, "value": 10, "unit": "x", "explanation": "350 ÷ 36 is about 9.7, so roughly tenfold in four years."}, {"kind": "spotFake", "id": "fake", "prompt": "One of these is false. Tap it.", "statements": ["OpenAI projected $278 billion of cash burn from 2026 to 2030.", "The Bank of England warned of a higher risk of a sharp correction.", "OpenAI expects compute to be its smallest cost through 2030."], "fakeIndex": 2, "explanation": "Compute and infrastructure, about $856 billion by 2030, is its largest expense."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "review", "prompt": "Week 6 review: at OpenAI in 2024, what share of R&D compute went to final training runs?", "options": ["About 10%", "About 50%", "About 90%"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "About $500 million of $5 billion. Most compute went to research and experiments."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Have a view on the gap", "body": "Be ready to say whether revenue can grow from $36 billion to $350 billion by 2030. It is the question behind the race.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.thestar.com.my/tech/tech-news/2026/09/19/openai-forecasts-cash-burn-near-280-billion-by-2030-ft-reports", "label": "Reuters via The Star, OpenAI forecasts cash burn near $280 billion by 2030, Sep 2026"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI, the arms race lasts only as long as revenue or investors keep paying for it.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.thestar.com.my/tech/tech-news/2026/09/19/openai-forecasts-cash-burn-near-280-billion-by-2030-ft-reports", "label": "Reuters via The Star, OpenAI forecasts cash burn near $280 billion by 2030, Sep 2026"}, {"url": "https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/financial-policy-committee-record/2025/october-2025", "label": "Bank of England, Financial Policy Committee record, Oct 2025"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "OpenAI projects $278 billion of cash burn through 2030 and about $856 billion of compute. The race depends on revenue growing about tenfold.", "sectionKey": "my_view"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
