label": "Stanford CRFM, Alpaca: a strong, replicable instruction-following model, Mar 2023"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In fine-tuning, a win rate means something only next to its judge and its reference.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://crfm.stanford.edu/2023/03/13/alpaca.html", "label": "Stanford CRFM, Alpaca: a strong, replicable instruction-following model, Mar 2023"}, {"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.04475", "label": "Dubois et al., Length-Controlled AlpacaEval, Apr 2024"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "A win rate counts head-to-head wins against a reference. Alpaca tied text-davinci-003 90 to 89 for under $600, but judges that favor long answers can inflate the number.", "sectionKey": "numbers"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$12a09f68-408e-56cd-b317-8615ba520086$ml$::uuid, $ml$ai$ml$, $ml$The one-third line$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-47$ml$, $ml$month-2$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "ai-d47-career", "title": "The one-third line", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "Change a model enough, and its legal duties become yours.", "eyebrow": "Day 47 · The rule", "headline": "Under EU guidelines from July 18, 2025, fine-tuning a general-purpose model with more than a third of its original training compute makes you its provider.", "fullText": "The European Commission's guidelines on general-purpose AI treat this as an indicative rule of thumb under the AI Act. Such a change counts as significant to the model's generality, capabilities or systemic risk. If the original compute is unknown, a fallback threshold based on the general criteria applies. Modest fine-tuning stays below the line.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.wilmerhale.com/en/insights/blogs/wilmerhale-privacy-and-cybersecurity-law/20250724-european-commission-issues-guidelines-for-providers-of-general-purpose-ai-models", "label": "WilmerHale, Commission guidelines for general-purpose AI providers, Jul 2025"}, {"url": "https://www.mayerbrown.com/en/insights/publications/2025/08/eu-ai-act-news-rules-on-general-purpose-ai-start-applying-guidelines-and-template-for-summary-of-training-data-finalized", "label": "Mayer Brown, EU AI Act rules on general-purpose AI start applying, Aug 2025"}, {"url": "https://cms.law/en/swe/legal-updates/general-purpose-ai-models-obligations-and-roles-for-providers-and-downstream-modifiers-under-the-eu-ai-act", "label": "CMS, providers and downstream modifiers under the EU AI Act, Jan 2026"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "below", "eyebrow": "Below the line", "text": "Modest fine-tuning that does not materially change what a model can do does not make you its provider.", "highlight": "InstructGPT's RLHF step used under 2% of GPT-3's pretraining compute.", "sources": [{"url": "https://cms.law/en/swe/legal-updates/general-purpose-ai-models-obligations-and-roles-for-providers-and-downstream-modifiers-under-the-eu-ai-act", "label": "CMS, providers and downstream modifiers under the EU AI Act, Jan 2026"}, {"url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2203.02155", "label": "Ouyang et al., Training language models to follow instructions with human feedback, 2022"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "above", "eyebrow": "Above the line", "text": "Cross it, and provider duties apply, but only to your modification.", "highlight": "Your documentation, data summary and copyright policy cover only what you added.", "sources": [{"url": "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/gpai-guidelines-overview/", "label": "artificialintelligenceact.eu, overview of the guidelines for GPAI models"}, {"url": "https://cms.law/en/swe/legal-updates/general-purpose-ai-models-obligations-and-roles-for-providers-and-downstream-modifiers-under-the-eu-ai-act", "label": "CMS, providers and downstream modifiers under the EU AI Act, Jan 2026"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "terms", "eyebrow": "The other rule", "title": "A model's terms bind fine-tuning too", "body": "Contracts can limit what you build from a model's outputs. OpenAI's terms prohibit developing models that compete with OpenAI.", "bullets": ["Partly for that reason, Stanford prohibited any commercial use of Alpaca."], "sources": [{"url": "https://crfm.stanford.edu/2023/03/13/alpaca.html", "label": "Stanford CRFM, Alpaca: a strong, replicable instruction-following model, Mar 2023"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-third", "prompt": "A model was trained with 9 units of compute. Above how many units does a fine-tune make you its provider?", "min": 0, "max": 10, "value": 3, "unit": "units", "explanation": "One third of 9 is 3. Use more than 3 units on the modification and you are presumed the new provider."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "What is the maximum fine for breaking the EU rules on general-purpose AI models?", "options": ["A flat €1 million per model", "Only written warnings, no fines", "Up to €15 million or 3% of revenue"], "correctIndex": 2, "explanation": "Up to €15 million or 3% of global revenue, whichever is higher."}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "Does each fine-tune make you the provider?", "buckets": ["Becomes the provider", "Stays a user"], "items": [{"text": "Retrains with half the original compute", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Retrains with 40% of the original compute", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "A modest fine-tune on support chats", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "RLHF using 2% of the original compute", "bucket": 1}], "explanation": "Above one third of the original compute you are presumed the provider. Light tuning stays below the line."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Know the one-third line", "body": "Fine-tuning with over a third of the original compute can make a company the provider in the EU. Legal and ML teams both need to know it.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.wilmerhale.com/en/insights/blogs/wilmerhale-privacy-and-cybersecurity-law/20250724-european-commission-issues-guidelines-for-providers-of-general-purpose-ai-models", "label": "WilmerHale, Commission guidelines for general-purpose AI providers, Jul 2025"}, {"url": "https://cms.law/en/swe/legal-updates/general-purpose-ai-models-obligations-and-roles-for-providers-and-downstream-modifiers-under-the-eu-ai-act", "label": "CMS, providers and downstream modifiers under the EU AI Act, Jan 2026"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In the EU, how much you change a model decides whether its duties become yours.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.wilmerhale.com/en/insights/blogs/wilmerhale-privacy-and-cybersecurity-law/20250724-european-commission-issues-guidelines-for-providers-of-general-purpose-ai-models", "label": "WilmerHale, Commission guidelines for general-purpose AI providers, Jul 2025"}, {"url": "https://cms.law/en/swe/legal-updates/general-purpose-ai-models-obligations-and-roles-for-providers-and-downstream-modifiers-under-the-eu-ai-act", "label": "CMS, providers and downstream modifiers under the EU AI Act, Jan 2026"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "EU guidelines from July 2025 make you a model's provider if your fine-tune uses more than a third of its original compute. Modest tuning stays below the line, and a model's terms can bind you too.", "sectionKey": "risk"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
