ou are presumed the new provider."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "What is the maximum fine for breaking the EU rules on general-purpose AI models?", "options": ["A flat €1 million per model", "Only written warnings, no fines", "Up to €15 million or 3% of revenue"], "correctIndex": 2, "explanation": "Up to €15 million or 3% of global revenue, whichever is higher."}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "Does each fine-tune make you the provider?", "buckets": ["Becomes the provider", "Stays a user"], "items": [{"text": "Retrains with half the original compute", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Retrains with 40% of the original compute", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "A modest fine-tune on support chats", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "RLHF using 2% of the original compute", "bucket": 1}], "explanation": "Above one third of the original compute you are presumed the provider. Light tuning stays below the line."}, {"id": "lens-invest", "kind": "info", "title": "Heavy tuning brings duties", "body": "A company that retrains a model deeply takes on provider duties in the EU, with fines up to €15 million or 3% of revenue.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.wilmerhale.com/en/insights/blogs/wilmerhale-privacy-and-cybersecurity-law/20250724-european-commission-issues-guidelines-for-providers-of-general-purpose-ai-models", "label": "WilmerHale, Commission guidelines for general-purpose AI providers, Jul 2025"}, {"url": "https://cms.law/en/swe/legal-updates/general-purpose-ai-models-obligations-and-roles-for-providers-and-downstream-modifiers-under-the-eu-ai-act", "label": "CMS, providers and downstream modifiers under the EU AI Act, Jan 2026"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In the EU, how much you change a model decides whether its duties become yours.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.wilmerhale.com/en/insights/blogs/wilmerhale-privacy-and-cybersecurity-law/20250724-european-commission-issues-guidel