t window", "A larger set of parameters", "Training on human feedback"], "correctIndex": 2, "explanation": "InstructGPT was trained on human feedback and won despite more than 100 times fewer parameters. OpenAI noted such behavior is hard to get through prompt engineering alone."}, {"id": "lens-invest", "kind": "info", "title": "Wording is easy to copy", "body": "A better prompt needs no training compute, so a rival can match it quickly. Look for advantages that outlast the wording.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2005.14165", "label": "Brown et al., Language models are few-shot learners, 2020"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI, the prompt is the cheapest lever: it changes the answer without changing the model.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2205.11916", "label": "Kojima et al., Large Language Models are Zero-Shot Reasoners, 2022"}, {"url": "https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2005.14165", "label": "Brown et al., Language models are few-shot learners, 2020"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Prompt engineering changes what you send a model, not the model. Five words lifted one math score from 17.7% to 78.7%, and everything has to fit in the context window.", "sectionKey": "watchlist"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
