d": "info", "title": "Caching shifts the margin", "body": "Repeated prompt text billed at a tenth of the price changes unit economics. Ask how much of a product's traffic can be cached.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing", "label": "Anthropic, Claude API pricing, Nov 2026"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI apps, every token you resend is billed again, so reuse is where the margin hides.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing", "label": "Anthropic, Claude API pricing, Nov 2026"}, {"url": "https://claude.com/resources/articles/prompt-caching", "label": "Anthropic, Prompt caching with Claude"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Developers pay per token, and output costs more than input. Caching bills repeated prompt text at a tenth of the price on most Claude models, which turns prompt design into a margin decision.", "sectionKey": "drivers"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
