odels.", "highlight": "A five-minute cache write costs 1.25 times, so it pays off after one reuse.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Prompt caching", "definition": "Storing the repeated start of a prompt so later requests read it cheaply."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing", "label": "Anthropic, Claude API pricing, Nov 2026"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "margin", "eyebrow": "Where the margin sits", "title": "Every repeated token is a cost line", "body": "An app pays for its instructions on every call. Caching and a 50% batch discount turn prompt design into a margin decision.", "bullets": ["OpenAI made caching automatic in October 2024, at half price on prompts over 1,024 tokens."], "sources": [{"url": "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing", "label": "Anthropic, Claude API pricing, Nov 2026"}, {"url": "https://openai.com/index/api-prompt-caching", "label": "OpenAI, Prompt caching in the API, Oct 2024"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-cache", "prompt": "A cache hit costs 0.1 times the input price. If input costs $3 per million tokens, what do a million cached tokens cost, in cents?", "min": 0, "max": 100, "value": 30, "unit": "cents", "explanation": "$3 times 0.1 is $0.30, the cache price Anthropic lists for Claude Sonnet 4.6."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "Your support bot sends the same 20,000-token manual with every customer question.", "prompt": "What cuts the bill first?", "options": ["Move to the priciest model for better answers", "Cache the manual so repeats cost a tenth", "Send the manual twice so it reads closely"], "consequences": ["A pricier model raises the cost of every token.", "Cache reads cost 0.1 times input on most Claude models.", "Twice the tokens means twice the input bill."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "The manual never changes, so it is the part to cache. The first write costs a little more, and every reuse after that costs far less."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "Why repeats get cheaper", "body": "Many apps resend the same instructions with every question. Caching lets them pay far less for the repeats.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://claude.com/resources/articles/prompt-caching", "label": "Anthropic, Prompt caching with Claude"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI apps, every token you resend is billed again, so reuse is where the margin hides.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing", "label": "Anthropic, Claude API pricing, Nov 2026"}, {"url": "https://claude.com/resources/articles/prompt-caching", "label": "Anthropic, Prompt caching with Claude"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Developers pay per token, and output costs more than input. Caching bills repeated prompt text at a tenth of the price on most Claude models, which turns prompt design into a margin decision.", "sectionKey": "chain"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$c0354db4-8be8-51b9-9747-5f484e698438$ml$::uuid, $ml$ai$ml$, $ml$Who controls what the model can see$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-51$ml$, $ml$month-2$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "ai-d51-career", "title": "Who controls what the model can see", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "A model only knows what someone lets it read.", "eyebrow": "Day 51 · The power", "headline": "In December 2025, Anthropic gave away MCP, a standard with more than 97 million monthly SDK downloads.", "fullText": "The Model Context Protocol, or MCP, is an open standard for connecting AI models to outside tools and data. On December 9, 2025, Anthropic donated it to the new Agentic AI Foundation, a fund under the Linux Foundation co-founded by Anthropic, Block and OpenAI. By then MCP had more than 10,000 active public servers, and ChatGPT, Gemini, Microsoft Copilot, Cursor and Visual Studio Code had adopted it.", "sources": [{"url": "https://anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation", "label": "Anthropic, Donating MCP and the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}, {"url": "https://blog.modelcontextprotocol.io/posts/2025-12-09-mcp-joins-agentic-ai-foundation/", "label": "MCP blog, MCP joins the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "pipe", "eyebrow": "The pipe", "text": "A model can only use what reaches its context window. Connectors carry outside data in.", "highlight": "MCP is an open standard for those connectors, now run by a neutral foundation.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "MCP", "definition": "Model Context Protocol, an open standard for linking AI models to tools and data."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation", "label": "Anthropic, Donating MCP and the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}, {"url": "https://blog.modelcontextprotocol.io/posts/2025-12-09-mcp-joins-agentic-ai-foundation/", "label": "MCP blog, MCP joins the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "owner", "eyebrow": "The owner", "text": "Whoever holds the data can still say no.", "highlight": "In 2025, Salesforce barred apps like Glean from storing or indexing Slack data long term.", "sources": [{"url": "https://cyprus-mail.com/2025/06/13/salesforce-blocks-ai-rivals-from-using-slack-data-according-to-reports", "label": "Reuters via Cyprus Mail, Salesforce blocks AI rivals from using Slack data, Jun 2025"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "leverage", "eyebrow": "Where leverage sits", "title": "Open pipes, closed taps", "body": "A shared standard makes connecting cheap for everyone. The data owner's terms still decide what flows.", "bullets": ["Slack's API terms now bar using that data in large language models."], "sources": [{"url": "https://natlawreview.com/article/salesforce-locks-down-slack-data-time-review-your-slack-api-terms", "label": "National Law Review, Salesforce locks down Slack data, Aug 2025"}, {"url": "https://anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation", "label": "Anthropic, Donating MCP and the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}]}, {"kind": "faceOff", "id": "face", "prompt": "Who can stop an AI assistant from indexing a company's Slack history?", "left": {"name": "The AI app maker", "note": "Builds the assistant"}, "right": {"name": "Salesforce, which owns Slack", "note": "Writes the API terms"}, "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Salesforce changed Slack's terms in 2025, and apps like Glean could no longer index or store that data long term."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "What does MCP standardize?", "options": ["How models connect to tools and data", "How models are trained on new data", "How model makers price each token"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "MCP is a shared way to plug models into outside tools and data. ChatGPT, Gemini and Copilot all adopted it."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "Your AI search startup indexes customers' Slack messages. Slack's terms just changed.", "prompt": "What do you do?", "options": ["Keep copying the data and hope nobody checks", "Wait for Salesforce to reverse the change", "Rebuild on data you are allowed to use"], "consequences": ["Breaking the terms risks losing access entirely.", "Your product stalls while you wait.", "The new terms bar persistent copies and indexes of Slack data."], "correctIndex": 2, "explanation": "The data owner sets the terms. A product built on data it cannot keep has to change its design."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Ask where the context comes from", "body": "Ask which data an AI product depends on and who controls it. One terms change can switch a feature off.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://cyprus-mail.com/2025/06/13/salesforce-blocks-ai-rivals-from-using-slack-data-according-to-reports", "label": "Reuters via Cyprus Mail, Salesforce blocks AI rivals from using Slack data, Jun 2025"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In AI apps, power sits with whoever controls the data that fills the context window.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://cyprus-mail.com/2025/06/13/salesforce-blocks-ai-rivals-from-using-slack-data-according-to-reports", "label": "Reuters via Cyprus Mail, Salesforce blocks AI rivals from using Slack data, Jun 2025"}, {"url": "https://anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation", "label": "Anthropic, Donating MCP and the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "MCP made connecting models to data an open standard with more than 97 million monthly SDK downloads. Data owners like Salesforce still decide what flows, so control of the context is control of the product.", "sectionKey": "questions"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
