iness model.", "highlight": "He wanted to avoid being locked into a competitor's closed ecosystem.", "sources": [{"url": "https://about.fb.com/news/2024/07/open-source-ai-is-the-path-forward/", "label": "Mark Zuckerberg, Open Source AI Is the Path Forward, Jul 2024"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "price", "eyebrow": "The price war", "title": "Open models push prices down", "body": "In April 2026, Artificial Analysis found top open models matched leading closed ones closely. They cost half to one sixth as much.", "bullets": ["Zuckerberg claimed Llama 3.1 405B could run at about half the cost of GPT-4o."], "sources": [{"url": "https://artificialanalysis.ai/articles/recent-open-weights-model-launches", "label": "Artificial Analysis, recent open weights model launches, Apr 2026"}, {"url": "https://about.fb.com/news/2024/07/open-source-ai-is-the-path-forward/", "label": "Mark Zuckerberg, Open Source AI Is the Path Forward, Jul 2024"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-arr", "prompt": "Mistral's run rate rose from $20 million to about $400 million in a year. How many times bigger is that?", "min": 0, "max": 50, "value": 20, "unit": "x", "explanation": "$400 million divided by $20 million is 20 times, in one year."}, {"kind": "faceOff", "id": "face", "prompt": "Which company says selling access to models is not its business?", "left": {"name": "Meta", "note": "Gives Llama weights away"}, "right": {"name": "Mistral", "note": "Sells AI to companies"}, "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Zuckerberg wrote that selling access to AI models is not Meta's business model. Mistral earns from paying customers."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "How does Mistral earn money while publishing free models?", "options": ["By charging for each download", "From companies that pay it for AI", "From a fee on every student user"], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Its paying customers include ASML, TotalEnergies and HSBC."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "Why give away something costly", "body": "Mistral sells services around free models. Meta gives models away so no rival controls the platform it builds on.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://about.fb.com/news/2024/07/open-source-ai-is-the-path-forward/", "label": "Mark Zuckerberg, Open Source AI Is the Path Forward, Jul 2024"}, {"url": "https://www.hl.co.uk/shares/stock-market-news/company--news/mistral-invests-in-swedish-infrastructure-as-annual-revenues-top-$400m", "label": "Sharecast via Hargreaves Lansdown, Mistral revenues top $400m, Feb 2026"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In open AI, the model is the free sample and the service is the product.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.hl.co.uk/shares/stock-market-news/company--news/mistral-invests-in-swedish-infrastructure-as-annual-revenues-top-$400m", "label": "Sharecast via Hargreaves Lansdown, Mistral revenues top $400m, Feb 2026"}, {"url": "https://about.fb.com/news/2024/07/open-source-ai-is-the-path-forward/", "label": "Mark Zuckerberg, Open Source AI Is the Path Forward, Jul 2024"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Mistral gives models away under Apache 2.0, yet its run rate grew from $20 million to over $400 million in a year. Open models earn through services, and they push prices down.", "sectionKey": "chain"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$13668372-6cd6-58ff-8fed-fbcd91c4a930$ml$::uuid, $ml$ai$ml$, $ml$The open model lead moved to China$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-57$ml$, $ml$month-2$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "ai-d57-career", "title": "The open model lead moved to China", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "Whoever others build on holds the power.", "eyebrow": "Day 57 · The power", "headline": "Hugging Face reported in March 2026 that Chinese models made up 41% of its downloads over the past year.", "fullText": "Hugging Face is the main site for sharing open models. In 2025 it grew to 13 million users and more than 2 million public models. Its report found China had passed the US in monthly and overall downloads, and the most liked models shifted from Meta's Llama family to a mix led by DeepSeek-R1.", "sources": [{"url": "https://huggingface.co/blog/huggingface/state-of-os-hf-spring-2026", "label": "Hugging Face, State of Open Source on Hugging Face: Spring 2026"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "qwen", "eyebrow": "The new base", "text": "In September 2025, Alibaba's Qwen passed Llama as the most downloaded model family on Hugging Face.", "highlight": "More than 113,000 models are built on Qwen.", "sources": [{"url": "https://hai.stanford.edu/assets/files/hai-digichina-issue-brief-beyond-deepseek-chinas-diverse-open-weight-ai-ecosystem-policy-implications.pdf", "label": "Stanford HAI and DigiChina, Beyond DeepSeek: China's open-weight AI ecosystem, Dec 2025"}, {"url": "https://huggingface.co/blog/huggingface/state-of-os-hf-spring-2026", "label": "Hugging Face, State of Open Source on Hugging Face: Spring 2026"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "usage", "eyebrow": "Real use", "text": "OpenRouter routes requests to many models. Over a year, Chinese open models averaged 13% of its weekly tokens.", "highlight": "In some weeks they neared 30% of all usage.", "sources": [{"url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.10088", "label": "a16z and OpenRouter, State of AI: a 100 trillion token study, Dec 2025"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "response", "eyebrow": "The response", "title": "The US wants its own open leaders", "body": "In July 2025, the White House AI Action Plan called for leading American open models. Meta still launched Muse Spark closed.", "bullets": ["The plan says the choice to release open or closed is up to the developer."], "sources": [{"url": "https://fedscoop.com/open-source-ai-trump-ai-action-plan/", "label": "FedScoop, open source in the AI Action Plan, Jul 2025"}, {"url": "https://www.artificialintelligence-news.com/news/meta-muse-spark-ai-model-open-source/", "label": "AI News, Meta launches Muse Spark as a proprietary model, Apr 2026"}]}, {"kind": "buildChain", "id": "chain", "prompt": "Put the shift in open models in order.", "steps": ["Meta releases Llama 3.1 405B with open weights", "Qwen passes Llama as the most downloaded family", "Hugging Face reports China at 41% of downloads", "Meta launches Muse Spark as a closed model"], "explanation": "July 2024, September 2025, March 2026, then April 2026."}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-qwen", "prompt": "About how many thousand models are built on Qwen, per Hugging Face?", "min": 0, "max": 300, "value": 113, "unit": "K", "explanation": "More than 113,000, and over 200,000 if you count every model tagged Qwen."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "You lead AI at a US retailer. The best open model for your task is Chinese.", "prompt": "What do you do?", "options": ["Ban it without testing it", "Test it on your own servers first", "Send customer data to its maker's API"], "consequences": ["You may give up a cost edge with no evidence.", "Self-hosted weights keep your data on your own machines.", "That sends customer data outside your control."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Open weights can run on your own hardware. You can judge the model without handing data to anyone."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Know who leads open models", "body": "Know that Chinese labs led open downloads by 2026. Saying Llama leads open AI is out of date.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://huggingface.co/blog/huggingface/state-of-os-hf-spring-2026", "label": "Hugging Face, State of Open Source on Hugging Face: Spring 2026"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In open AI, power goes to whoever everyone else builds on.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://huggingface.co/blog/huggingface/state-of-os-hf-spring-2026", "label": "Hugging Face, State of Open Source on Hugging Face: Spring 2026"}, {"url": "https://hai.stanford.edu/assets/files/hai-digichina-issue-brief-beyond-deepseek-chinas-diverse-open-weight-ai-ecosystem-policy-implications.pdf", "label": "Stanford HAI and DigiChina, Beyond DeepSeek: China's open-weight AI ecosystem, Dec 2025"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "By March 2026, Chinese models made up 41% of Hugging Face downloads, and over 113,000 models build on Qwen. In open AI, power follows what others build on.", "sectionKey": "questions"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
