ur app.", "prompt": "What do you check first?", "options": ["If its license lets EU firms use it", "How many stars its code page has", "Whether its logo suits your brand"], "consequences": ["Llama 4 barred companies based in the EU at launch.", "Popularity says nothing about your rights.", "A logo matters far less than legal access."], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "An open model is only open to you if its license says so. Read it before you build."}, {"id": "lens-invest", "kind": "info", "title": "License terms shape the market", "body": "A license that excludes EU firms or the largest companies shrinks who can sell products built on it.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/04/05/meta-releases-llama-4-a-new-crop-of-flagship-ai-models", "label": "TechCrunch, Meta releases Llama 4, Apr 2025"}, {"url": "https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-4-Maverick-17B-128E-Original", "label": "Meta, Llama 4 Maverick model card and license"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In open AI, the license decides who may use the model, and how.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-4-Maverick-17B-128E-Original", "label": "Meta, Llama 4 Maverick model card and license"}, {"url": "https://hai.stanford.edu/assets/files/hai-digichina-issue-brief-beyond-deepseek-chinas-diverse-open-weight-ai-ecosystem-policy-implications.pdf", "label": "Stanford HAI and DigiChina, Beyond DeepSeek: China's open-weight AI ecosystem, Dec 2025"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Llama 4's license requires permission above 700 million monthly users and a Built with Llama label, and it kept EU firms out at launch. Qwen3 and DeepSeek-R1 use standard licenses.", "sectionKey": "risk"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
