for your app.", "prompt": "What do you check first?", "options": ["If its license lets EU firms use it", "How many stars its code page has", "Whether its logo suits your brand"], "consequences": ["Llama 4 barred companies based in the EU at launch.", "Popularity says nothing about your rights.", "A logo matters far less than legal access."], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "An open model is only open to you if its license says so. Read it before you build."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "Open comes in degrees", "body": "Some open models come with almost no strings, others with many. Llama 4 even sets how derived models must be named.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-4-Maverick-17B-128E-Original", "label": "Meta, Llama 4 Maverick model card and license"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In open AI, the license decides who may use the model, and how.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-4-Maverick-17B-128E-Original", "label": "Meta, Llama 4 Maverick model card and license"}, {"url": "https://hai.stanford.edu/assets/files/hai-digichina-issue-brief-beyond-deepseek-chinas-diverse-open-weight-ai-ecosystem-policy-implications.pdf", "label": "Stanford HAI and DigiChina, Beyond DeepSeek: China's open-weight AI ecosystem, Dec 2025"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Llama 4's license requires permission above 700 million monthly users and a Built with Llama label, and it kept EU firms out at launch. Qwen3 and DeepSeek-R1 use standard licenses.", "sectionKey": "rules"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b52129e2-282c-5dc4-95bc-8298f8af87c5$ml$::uuid, $ml$ai$ml$, $ml$Weights cannot be recalled$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-60$ml$, $ml$month-2$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "ai-d60-career", "title": "Weights cannot be recalled", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "Once the weights are out, they stay out.", "eyebrow": "Day 60 · Where it breaks", "headline": "On October 15, 2026, Meta released the weights of Muse Spark Open, an 816-billion-parameter model.", "fullText": "Earlier in 2026, Meta had declined to release Muse Spark's weights, citing safety concerns. The open version got extra safety training first. Meta still cautioned that changes made downstream could degrade its safety. A US government report notes that once weights are downloaded, developers cannot rescind access to them.", "sources": [{"url": "https://unite.ai/metas-816b-parameter-muse-spark-open-weights-are-now-public", "label": "Unite.AI, Meta's Muse Spark Open weights are public, Oct 2026"}, {"url": "https://eweek.com/news/news-meta-open-weight-ai-strategy", "label": "eWeek, Meta reopens its AI models, Aug 2026"}, {"url": "https://www.ntia.gov/programs-and-initiatives/artificial-intelligence/open-model-weights-report/background", "label": "NTIA, open model weights report, background"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "cheap", "eyebrow": "Cheap to undo", "text": "In 2023, researchers undid the safety training of Meta's Llama 2-Chat 13B for less than $200.", "highlight": "They concluded safety fine-tuning cannot stop misuse once weights are public.", "sources": [{"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.00117v3", "label": "Gade et al., BadLlama: cheaply removing safety fine-tuning from Llama 2-Chat 13B, 2023"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "gpu", "eyebrow": "One GPU", "text": "Another team did the same to Llama 2-Chat 70B, using one GPU and under $200 per model.", "highlight": "Its refusal rate fell below 1% on two refusal tests.", "sources": [{"url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2310.20624", "label": "Lermen et al., LoRA fine-tuning undoes safety training in Llama 2-Chat 70B, 2023"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "test", "eyebrow": "The new test", "title": "OpenAI tested the worst case first", "body": "Before gpt-oss shipped, OpenAI tuned it to drop refusals on biology and cyber, as an attacker might. It still fell short of High capability.", "bullets": ["Three independent expert groups reviewed the method."], "sources": [{"url": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-oss/", "label": "OpenAI, Introducing gpt-oss, Aug 2025"}]}, {"kind": "faceOff", "id": "face", "prompt": "Which can its maker still pull back after release?", "left": {"name": "A closed model", "note": "Runs only on the lab's servers"}, "right": {"name": "An open-weight model", "note": "Weights downloaded by anyone"}, "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A lab can stop serving a closed model. Downloaded weights can be shared on, and access cannot be rescinded."}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-cost", "prompt": "Researchers undid Llama 2-Chat 13B's safety training for under how many dollars?", "min": 0, "max": 1000, "value": 200, "unit": "$", "explanation": "Less than $200. A second team undid the 70B model for under $200 on one GPU."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "You run a lab about to publish a model's weights.", "prompt": "What should come first?", "options": ["Test it with its safety stripped out", "Release it and patch problems later", "Trust its built-in refusals to hold"], "consequences": ["That is the test OpenAI ran before gpt-oss.", "You cannot patch copies on other people's machines.", "Safety training was undone for under $200 in 2023."], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A release is permanent. Testing the worst case first is the only chance to catch it."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Know the open safety debate", "body": "Be ready to explain why released weights are hard to secure. Safety training on Llama 2 was undone for under $200.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.00117v3", "label": "Gade et al., BadLlama: cheaply removing safety fine-tuning from Llama 2-Chat 13B, 2023"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In open AI, a release is permanent, so test the worst case before you ship.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.ntia.gov/programs-and-initiatives/artificial-intelligence/open-model-weights-report/background", "label": "NTIA, open model weights report, background"}, {"url": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-oss/", "label": "OpenAI, Introducing gpt-oss, Aug 2025"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Meta released Muse Spark Open in October 2026, and released weights cannot be recalled. Safety training was undone for under $200 in 2023, so OpenAI tested a worst case fine-tune of gpt-oss before release.", "sectionKey": "my_view"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
