 70B, using one GPU and under $200 per model.", "highlight": "Its refusal rate fell below 1% on two refusal tests.", "sources": [{"url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2310.20624", "label": "Lermen et al., LoRA fine-tuning undoes safety training in Llama 2-Chat 70B, 2023"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "test", "eyebrow": "The new test", "title": "OpenAI tested the worst case first", "body": "Before gpt-oss shipped, OpenAI tuned it to drop refusals on biology and cyber, as an attacker might. It still fell short of High capability.", "bullets": ["Three independent expert groups reviewed the method."], "sources": [{"url": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-oss/", "label": "OpenAI, Introducing gpt-oss, Aug 2025"}]}, {"kind": "faceOff", "id": "face", "prompt": "Which can its maker still pull back after release?", "left": {"name": "A closed model", "note": "Runs only on the lab's servers"}, "right": {"name": "An open-weight model", "note": "Weights downloaded by anyone"}, "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A lab can stop serving a closed model. Downloaded weights can be shared on, and access cannot be rescinded."}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-cost", "prompt": "Researchers undid Llama 2-Chat 13B's safety training for under how many dollars?", "min": 0, "max": 1000, "value": 200, "unit": "$", "explanation": "Less than $200. A second team undid the 70B model for under $200 on one GPU."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "You run a lab about to publish a model's weights.", "prompt": "What should come first?", "options": ["Test it with its safety stripped out", "Release it and patch problems later", "Trust its built-in refusals to hold"], "consequences": ["That is the test OpenAI ran before gpt-oss.", "You cannot patch copies on other people's machines.", "Safety training was undone for under $200 in 2023."], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A release is permanent. Testing the worst case first is the only chance to catch it."}, {"id": "lens-invest", "kind": "info", "title": "Release strategy can flip", "body": "Meta kept Muse Spark closed in April 2026, then released open weights in October. A lab's stance on openness can change fast.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.artificialintelligence-news.com/news/meta-muse-spark-ai-model-open-source/", "label": "AI News, Meta launches Muse Spark as a proprietary model, Apr 2026"}, {"url": "https://unite.ai/metas-816b-parameter-muse-spark-open-weights-are-now-public", "label": "Unite.AI, Meta's Muse Spark Open weights are public, Oct 2026"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In open AI, a release is permanent, so test the worst case before you ship.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.ntia.gov/programs-and-initiatives/artificial-intelligence/open-model-weights-report/background", "label": "NTIA, open model weights report, background"}, {"url": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-oss/", "label": "OpenAI, Introducing gpt-oss, Aug 2025"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Meta released Muse Spark Open in October 2026, and released weights cannot be recalled. Safety training was undone for under $200 in 2023, so OpenAI tested a worst case fine-tune of gpt-oss before release.", "sectionKey": "review"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
