($ml$c0e5607c-5e2d-5823-9c57-5e79acf636bd$ml$::uuid, $ml$3b0042fd-b31c-5a07-93f0-3388f4542ee5$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$GPT keeps half of the 2017 design$ml$, $ml$The 2017 Transformer had an encoder and a decoder, six layers each. GPT trains the decoder alone to predict the next word. The decoder's mask lets each prediction see only the words before it.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/html/1706.03762v7", "label": "Vaswani et al., Attention Is All You Need, 2017"}, {"url": "https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/model_doc/openai-gpt", "label": "Hugging Face Transformers docs, OpenAI GPT"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b5710637-90f6-5dd1-a731-79438d99a066$ml$::uuid, $ml$3b0042fd-b31c-5a07-93f0-3388f4542ee5$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Fine-tune, do not start over$ml$, $ml$Since 2018, the pattern has been to pre-train once and fine-tune for each task. Most startups build at the fine-tune end.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://openai.com/index/language-unsupervised/", "label": "OpenAI, Improving language understanding with unsupervised learning, Jun 2018"}]$ml$::jsonb),
