($ml$e0f6623c-324b-5d19-8c54-66482aef97e1$ml$::uuid, $ml$925c6b1f-7aaf-584f-94e9-61a5856a935c$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 36 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In February 2025, OpenAI launched GPT-4.5, its largest model, at $75 per million input tokens. That was 30 times GPT-4o's $2.50. GPT-4.5 scaled up pre-training, the recipe behind every earlier GPT, yet trailed reasoning models on hard math and science tests. In April 2025, OpenAI said it would pull GPT-4.5 from its API by July 14, because GPT-4.1 matched or beat it in key areas for much less.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/27/openai-unveils-gpt-4-5-orion-its-largest-ai-model-yet", "label": "TechCrunch, OpenAI unveils GPT-4.5, Feb 2025"}, {"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/04/14/openai-plans-to-wind-down-gpt-4-5-its-largest-ever-ai-model-in-its-api", "label": "TechCrunch, OpenAI to wind down GPT-4.5 in its API, Apr 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
