($ml$a44b7278-ea16-5c80-b523-555907feeca6$ml$::uuid, $ml$b50e0de7-a11e-5d19-8dc3-dc7e3c083dbd$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In AI, the bill for the biggest training run multiplies every year.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://epoch.ai/publications/how-much-does-it-cost-to-train-frontier-ai-models", "label": "Epoch AI, How much does it cost to train frontier AI models?, Jun 2024"}, {"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.21015", "label": "Cottier et al., The rising costs of training frontier AI models, 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7192b29c-4543-5835-9415-6fbc1751358b$ml$::uuid, $ml$8d21286d-c4fd-5bdf-8db1-145b474fb58f$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 41 · The rules$ml$, $ml$Since January 1, 2026, California's SB 53 has applied to AI models trained with more than 10^26 operations. Governor Newsom signed the Transparency in Frontier Artificial Intelligence Act on September 29, 2025. The count includes the original run plus later fine-tuning and reinforcement learning. Developers must publish a transparency report before deploying a new frontier model and report critical safety incidents within 15 days. Penalties reach $1 million.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b99134d9-75a0-55af-9b85-1a1d728c7367$ml$::uuid, $ml$8d21286d-c4fd-5bdf-8db1-145b474fb58f$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The big developers$ml$, $ml$Some duties apply only to developers with more than $500 million in revenue. They must publish a framework for how they manage catastrophic risk.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$9747face-bd6e-57ff-a894-20d4489776a5$ml$::uuid, $ml$8d21286d-c4fd-5bdf-8db1-145b474fb58f$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The EU line$ml$, $ml$The EU draws its line ten times lower, at 10^25 operations. Above it, a model is presumed to carry systemic risk.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$2edfc43f-88ed-5b18-a380-490c37ab0e3c$ml$::uuid, $ml$8d21286d-c4fd-5bdf-8db1-145b474fb58f$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Over 30 models had crossed 10^25$ml$, $ml$By June 2025, over 30 announced models from 12 developers had passed 10^25. GPT-4 was the first, in March 2023. Training at that scale costs tens of millions of dollars.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://epoch.ai/data-insights/models-over-1e25-flop", "label": "Epoch AI, Models over 10^25 FLOP"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$4405fa3c-05f4-5daf-871f-8273f0b54b77$ml$::uuid, $ml$8d21286d-c4fd-5bdf-8db1-145b474fb58f$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Know both compute lines$ml$, $ml$California starts at 10^26 operations, the EU at 10^25. Policy and safety teams track where each new model lands.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2025/10/Californias-Transparency-in-Frontier-Artificial-Intelligence-Act-5-Things-You-Should-Know", "label": "Orrick, California's Transparency in Frontier AI Act: 5 things to know, Oct 2025"}, {"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]$ml$::jsonb),
