($ml$3cb680b3-21f0-50c7-9fa3-cc93ca378f18$ml$::uuid, $ml$8b3807df-5c09-5564-af3d-5cb0db6e6e54$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Revenue has to grow tenfold$ml$, $ml$OpenAI's plan needs revenue to rise from $36 billion to $350 billion by 2030. Revenue would total about $840 billion, against $856 billion of compute.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.thestar.com.my/tech/tech-news/2026/09/19/openai-forecasts-cash-burn-near-280-billion-by-2030-ft-reports", "label": "Reuters via The Star, OpenAI forecasts cash burn near $280 billion by 2030, Sep 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$be0d2322-e1fc-55a9-9e0a-16585153c769$ml$::uuid, $ml$8b3807df-5c09-5564-af3d-5cb0db6e6e54$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$A tenfold bet$ml$, $ml$OpenAI expects to burn $278 billion from 2026 to 2030, betting its revenue grows about tenfold.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.thestar.com.my/tech/tech-news/2026/09/19/openai-forecasts-cash-burn-near-280-billion-by-2030-ft-reports", "label": "Reuters via The Star, OpenAI forecasts cash burn near $280 billion by 2030, Sep 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$a9e175e7-eab8-59a6-8ddc-6e29fd1d63f7$ml$::uuid, $ml$8b3807df-5c09-5564-af3d-5cb0db6e6e54$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In AI, the arms race lasts only as long as revenue or investors keep paying for it.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.thestar.com.my/tech/tech-news/2026/09/19/openai-forecasts-cash-burn-near-280-billion-by-2030-ft-reports", "label": "Reuters via The Star, OpenAI forecasts cash burn near $280 billion by 2030, Sep 2026"}, {"url": "https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/financial-policy-committee-record/2025/october-2025", "label": "Bank of England, Financial Policy Committee record, Oct 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$ca51f3ed-6273-55f9-932b-f1ae319c0e1b$ml$::uuid, $ml$504eca7a-18cf-599c-94c9-7493c2c83ed6$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 43 · Fine-tuning$ml$, $ml$In 2022, people preferred answers from a 1.3-billion-parameter model to those of the 175-billion-parameter GPT-3. OpenAI trained GPT-3 further on what people wanted and called the result InstructGPT. Labelers preferred the outputs of its 1.3 billion parameter version to those of the original 175 billion parameter GPT-3, despite 100 times fewer parameters. Size did not make the difference. The training after pretraining did: answers written by people, then their rankings of answers.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2203.02155", "label": "Ouyang et al., Training language models to follow instructions with human feedback, 2022"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$079dba6e-bb6e-5e65-a456-c18a2d72fa51$ml$::uuid, $ml$504eca7a-18cf-599c-94c9-7493c2c83ed6$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$Step one$ml$, $ml$First, people write good answers to prompts, and the model trains on them. InstructGPT's supervised fine-tuning set held about 13,000 training prompts.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2203.02155", "label": "Ouyang et al., Training language models to follow instructions with human feedback, 2022"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$d0cbc2e6-ef37-5002-8909-19fd4f9f73e0$ml$::uuid, $ml$504eca7a-18cf-599c-94c9-7493c2c83ed6$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$Steps two and three$ml$, $ml$Next, people rank several answers, and a reward model learns their taste. The model then trains to score well on it. That loop is reinforcement learning from human feedback, or RLHF.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2203.02155", "label": "Ouyang et al., Training language models to follow instructions with human feedback, 2022"}]$ml$::jsonb),
