($ml$931b4052-d21a-5d57-aad1-1319d8923445$ml$::uuid, $ml$aea94a50-c99a-55f6-ace6-6b1564c2ee6b$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 46 · The numbers$ml$, $ml$In March 2023, Stanford fine-tuned a 7-billion-parameter model for under $600. In blind tests it won 90 matchups to 89 against OpenAI's text-davinci-003. Stanford's Alpaca started from Meta's LLaMA 7B. The team generated 52,000 instruction-following examples with text-davinci-003 for less than $500, then fine-tuned for 3 hours on eight A100 GPUs for less than $100. They judged it with a blind pairwise comparison against the OpenAI model.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://crfm.stanford.edu/2023/03/13/alpaca.html", "label": "Stanford CRFM, Alpaca: a strong, replicable instruction-following model, Mar 2023"}]$ml$::jsonb),
