($ml$5434b00c-ac94-5d2c-8003-7b1743d98ebb$ml$::uuid, $ml$79d88960-a213-5bb0-99c4-02505cc488c9$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Most fine-tunes stay light$ml$, $ml$Light fine-tuning leaves the duties with the original provider. Check the model's terms too: some bar building rivals.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cms.law/en/swe/legal-updates/general-purpose-ai-models-obligations-and-roles-for-providers-and-downstream-modifiers-under-the-eu-ai-act", "label": "CMS, providers and downstream modifiers under the EU AI Act, Jan 2026"}, {"url": "https://crfm.stanford.edu/2023/03/13/alpaca.html", "label": "Stanford CRFM, Alpaca: a strong, replicable instruction-following model, Mar 2023"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$87082e9d-1fb0-52ba-af0e-e5df64236487$ml$::uuid, $ml$79d88960-a213-5bb0-99c4-02505cc488c9$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In the EU, how much you change a model decides whether its duties become yours.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.wilmerhale.com/en/insights/blogs/wilmerhale-privacy-and-cybersecurity-law/20250724-european-commission-issues-guidelines-for-providers-of-general-purpose-ai-models", "label": "WilmerHale, Commission guidelines for general-purpose AI providers, Jul 2025"}, {"url": "https://cms.law/en/swe/legal-updates/general-purpose-ai-models-obligations-and-roles-for-providers-and-downstream-modifiers-under-the-eu-ai-act", "label": "CMS, providers and downstream modifiers under the EU AI Act, Jan 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$5cadf8a1-e2a8-564a-bace-c7dfd9475797$ml$::uuid, $ml$0e9b88b4-fcd6-59a2-90a9-e847af1d06cf$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 47 · The rule$ml$, $ml$Under EU guidelines from July 18, 2025, fine-tuning a general-purpose model with more than a third of its original training compute makes you its provider. The European Commission's guidelines on general-purpose AI treat this as an indicative rule of thumb under the AI Act. Such a change counts as significant to the model's generality, capabilities or systemic risk. If the original compute is unknown, a fallback threshold based on the general criteria applies. Modest fine-tuning stays below the line.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.wilmerhale.com/en/insights/blogs/wilmerhale-privacy-and-cybersecurity-law/20250724-european-commission-issues-guidelines-for-providers-of-general-purpose-ai-models", "label": "WilmerHale, Commission guidelines for general-purpose AI providers, Jul 2025"}, {"url": "https://www.mayerbrown.com/en/insights/publications/2025/08/eu-ai-act-news-rules-on-general-purpose-ai-start-applying-guidelines-and-template-for-summary-of-training-data-finalized", "label": "Mayer Brown, EU AI Act rules on general-purpose AI start applying, Aug 2025"}, {"url": "https://cms.law/en/swe/legal-updates/general-purpose-ai-models-obligations-and-roles-for-providers-and-downstream-modifiers-under-the-eu-ai-act", "label": "CMS, providers and downstream modifiers under the EU AI Act, Jan 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$a43158e6-2f3e-522b-8136-b2e238e67049$ml$::uuid, $ml$0e9b88b4-fcd6-59a2-90a9-e847af1d06cf$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$Below the line$ml$, $ml$Modest fine-tuning that does not materially change what a model can do does not make you its provider. InstructGPT's RLHF step used under 2% of GPT-3's pretraining compute.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cms.law/en/swe/legal-updates/general-purpose-ai-models-obligations-and-roles-for-providers-and-downstream-modifiers-under-the-eu-ai-act", "label": "CMS, providers and downstream modifiers under the EU AI Act, Jan 2026"}, {"url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2203.02155", "label": "Ouyang et al., Training language models to follow instructions with human feedback, 2022"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$eb4cdb13-b5ee-59cf-b67b-6cf54d89199a$ml$::uuid, $ml$0e9b88b4-fcd6-59a2-90a9-e847af1d06cf$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$Above the line$ml$, $ml$Cross it, and provider duties apply, but only to your modification. Your documentation, data summary and copyright policy cover only what you added.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/gpai-guidelines-overview/", "label": "artificialintelligenceact.eu, overview of the guidelines for GPAI models"}, {"url": "https://cms.law/en/swe/legal-updates/general-purpose-ai-models-obligations-and-roles-for-providers-and-downstream-modifiers-under-the-eu-ai-act", "label": "CMS, providers and downstream modifiers under the EU AI Act, Jan 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$68c4abc7-4347-50a2-9435-0286562cbf1e$ml$::uuid, $ml$0e9b88b4-fcd6-59a2-90a9-e847af1d06cf$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$A model's terms bind fine-tuning too$ml$, $ml$Contracts can limit what you build from a model's outputs. OpenAI's terms prohibit developing models that compete with OpenAI. Partly for that reason, Stanford prohibited any commercial use of Alpaca.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://crfm.stanford.edu/2023/03/13/alpaca.html", "label": "Stanford CRFM, Alpaca: a strong, replicable instruction-following model, Mar 2023"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$f0f7c536-d36b-5238-91d1-8a492e1b61db$ml$::uuid, $ml$0e9b88b4-fcd6-59a2-90a9-e847af1d06cf$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$A third makes it yours$ml$, $ml$In the EU, retrain a model with over a third of its original compute and the rules treat you as its provider.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.wilmerhale.com/en/insights/blogs/wilmerhale-privacy-and-cybersecurity-law/20250724-european-commission-issues-guidelines-for-providers-of-general-purpose-ai-models", "label": "WilmerHale, Commission guidelines for general-purpose AI providers, Jul 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$2dec50a8-6c06-59d0-b275-7498bdcd37cb$ml$::uuid, $ml$0e9b88b4-fcd6-59a2-90a9-e847af1d06cf$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In the EU, how much you change a model decides whether its duties become yours.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.wilmerhale.com/en/insights/blogs/wilmerhale-privacy-and-cybersecurity-law/20250724-european-commission-issues-guidelines-for-providers-of-general-purpose-ai-models", "label": "WilmerHale, Commission guidelines for general-purpose AI providers, Jul 2025"}, {"url": "https://cms.law/en/swe/legal-updates/general-purpose-ai-models-obligations-and-roles-for-providers-and-downstream-modifiers-under-the-eu-ai-act", "label": "CMS, providers and downstream modifiers under the EU AI Act, Jan 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7effa8d3-cf3d-5a49-80d6-3136e56b20a6$ml$::uuid, $ml$bf0968f3-d62d-5862-b538-966f684b57db$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 48 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In May 2026, OpenAI began winding down its fine-tuning platform. New training jobs end for every customer by January 2027. OpenAI said newer base models like GPT-5.5 are much better at following instructions and formats than earlier ones. It said prompt-based approaches are now cheaper and faster, and that it sees fewer use cases that require fine-tuning. Fine-tuned models keep running until their base models are deprecated.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://openai.com/index/gpt-4o-fine-tuning/", "label": "OpenAI, Fine-tuning now available for GPT-4o, Aug 2024"}, {"url": "https://tessl.io/blog/openai-shutting-fine-tuning-signals-for-enterprise-ai", "label": "Tessl, OpenAI shutting down fine-tuning, May 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$d2201619-cba8-55d0-ad9e-6364e943e247$ml$::uuid, $ml$bf0968f3-d62d-5862-b538-966f684b57db$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$Why it changed$ml$, $ml$Instruction following moved into the base model. A prompt can now do much of what a fine-tune did. OpenAI opened GPT-4o fine-tuning in August 2024 and closed it to new users in May 2026.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://openai.com/index/gpt-4o-fine-tuning/", "label": "OpenAI, Fine-tuning now available for GPT-4o, Aug 2024"}, {"url": "https://tessl.io/blog/openai-shutting-fine-tuning-signals-for-enterprise-ai", "label": "Tessl, OpenAI shutting down fine-tuning, May 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$243b4e7e-6ac5-5f44-829c-7202d492bdac$ml$::uuid, $ml$bf0968f3-d62d-5862-b538-966f684b57db$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$Still broken$ml$, $ml$Feedback training still teaches models to tell users what they want to hear. A 2023 study found five leading AI assistants consistently sycophantic.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2310.13548", "label": "Sharma et al., Towards understanding sycophancy in language models, Oct 2023"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$430cbc47-7c32-5f64-b3c7-964130f72dbd$ml$::uuid, $ml$bf0968f3-d62d-5862-b538-966f684b57db$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Fine-tuning moves elsewhere$ml$, $ml$Google and Anthropic still offer managed fine-tuning to enterprise customers. Open models can still be tuned with methods like LoRA. OpenAI cuts off customers who have not used a tuned model in 60 days.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://tessl.io/blog/openai-shutting-fine-tuning-signals-for-enterprise-ai", "label": "Tessl, OpenAI shutting down fine-tuning, May 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$22e3fbe4-84b6-5db3-b1f2-a47495ed7ea5$ml$::uuid, $ml$bf0968f3-d62d-5862-b538-966f684b57db$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Know when not to fine-tune$ml$, $ml$OpenAI now says prompting newer models is cheaper and faster for most needs. Be ready to say when a prompt beats a fine-tune.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://tessl.io/blog/openai-shutting-fine-tuning-signals-for-enterprise-ai", "label": "Tessl, OpenAI shutting down fine-tuning, May 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$9ac6dd18-4e5d-50af-9194-ee297c395c40$ml$::uuid, $ml$bf0968f3-d62d-5862-b538-966f684b57db$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In AI, the better base models follow instructions, the less often fine-tuning is worth it.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://tessl.io/blog/openai-shutting-fine-tuning-signals-for-enterprise-ai", "label": "Tessl, OpenAI shutting down fine-tuning, May 2026"}, {"url": "https://openai.com/index/gpt-4o-fine-tuning/", "label": "OpenAI, Fine-tuning now available for GPT-4o, Aug 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
