($ml$eb9f9650-d972-5023-91eb-bbbe2d89227a$ml$::uuid, $ml$d2cbf4a2-0aa4-5ea9-8875-144bd0cf220d$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The owner$ml$, $ml$Whoever holds the data can still say no. In 2025, Salesforce barred apps like Glean from storing or indexing Slack data long term.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cyprus-mail.com/2025/06/13/salesforce-blocks-ai-rivals-from-using-slack-data-according-to-reports", "label": "Reuters via Cyprus Mail, Salesforce blocks AI rivals from using Slack data, Jun 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$ab015480-608a-58f2-a8ad-a5bc66e4847a$ml$::uuid, $ml$d2cbf4a2-0aa4-5ea9-8875-144bd0cf220d$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Open pipes, closed taps$ml$, $ml$A shared standard makes connecting cheap for everyone. The data owner's terms still decide what flows. Slack's API terms now bar using that data in large language models.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://natlawreview.com/article/salesforce-locks-down-slack-data-time-review-your-slack-api-terms", "label": "National Law Review, Salesforce locks down Slack data, Aug 2025"}, {"url": "https://anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation", "label": "Anthropic, Donating MCP and the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7a7cbc9e-f2c7-5cc2-bcde-a684301defca$ml$::uuid, $ml$d2cbf4a2-0aa4-5ea9-8875-144bd0cf220d$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Standards lower the toll$ml$, $ml$MCP lets any app plug into many tools the same way. The scarce part is data owners will let you use.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation", "label": "Anthropic, Donating MCP and the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}, {"url": "https://natlawreview.com/article/salesforce-locks-down-slack-data-time-review-your-slack-api-terms", "label": "National Law Review, Salesforce locks down Slack data, Aug 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$83e25eed-3751-54b6-aa07-b5d6817f16a6$ml$::uuid, $ml$d2cbf4a2-0aa4-5ea9-8875-144bd0cf220d$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In AI apps, power sits with whoever controls the data that fills the context window.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cyprus-mail.com/2025/06/13/salesforce-blocks-ai-rivals-from-using-slack-data-according-to-reports", "label": "Reuters via Cyprus Mail, Salesforce blocks AI rivals from using Slack data, Jun 2025"}, {"url": "https://anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation", "label": "Anthropic, Donating MCP and the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$939014a7-b225-5152-8251-a41aa07f6b56$ml$::uuid, $ml$aa123d55-36fe-5ef1-b815-63992329275a$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 51 · The power$ml$, $ml$In December 2025, Anthropic gave away MCP, a standard with more than 97 million monthly SDK downloads. The Model Context Protocol, or MCP, is an open standard for connecting AI models to outside tools and data. On December 9, 2025, Anthropic donated it to the new Agentic AI Foundation, a fund under the Linux Foundation co-founded by Anthropic, Block and OpenAI. By then MCP had more than 10,000 active public servers, and ChatGPT, Gemini, Microsoft Copilot, Cursor and Visual Studio Code had adopted it.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation", "label": "Anthropic, Donating MCP and the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}, {"url": "https://blog.modelcontextprotocol.io/posts/2025-12-09-mcp-joins-agentic-ai-foundation/", "label": "MCP blog, MCP joins the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$9b0f4046-dd27-5e21-8086-6a9accfdf981$ml$::uuid, $ml$aa123d55-36fe-5ef1-b815-63992329275a$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The pipe$ml$, $ml$A model can only use what reaches its context window. Connectors carry outside data in. MCP is an open standard for those connectors, now run by a neutral foundation.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation", "label": "Anthropic, Donating MCP and the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}, {"url": "https://blog.modelcontextprotocol.io/posts/2025-12-09-mcp-joins-agentic-ai-foundation/", "label": "MCP blog, MCP joins the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$0f00b1db-faa3-5a37-944c-fa4f5fd26961$ml$::uuid, $ml$aa123d55-36fe-5ef1-b815-63992329275a$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The owner$ml$, $ml$Whoever holds the data can still say no. In 2025, Salesforce barred apps like Glean from storing or indexing Slack data long term.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cyprus-mail.com/2025/06/13/salesforce-blocks-ai-rivals-from-using-slack-data-according-to-reports", "label": "Reuters via Cyprus Mail, Salesforce blocks AI rivals from using Slack data, Jun 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$321aa4de-a5ea-5d4a-aee0-123321fe8b5a$ml$::uuid, $ml$aa123d55-36fe-5ef1-b815-63992329275a$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Open pipes, closed taps$ml$, $ml$A shared standard makes connecting cheap for everyone. The data owner's terms still decide what flows. Slack's API terms now bar using that data in large language models.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://natlawreview.com/article/salesforce-locks-down-slack-data-time-review-your-slack-api-terms", "label": "National Law Review, Salesforce locks down Slack data, Aug 2025"}, {"url": "https://anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation", "label": "Anthropic, Donating MCP and the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$bea932e5-b276-59d4-97d7-260aa2ed984f$ml$::uuid, $ml$aa123d55-36fe-5ef1-b815-63992329275a$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$The model is not the whole story$ml$, $ml$An assistant only knows what it is allowed to read. Who controls that access shapes what AI can do for you.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cyprus-mail.com/2025/06/13/salesforce-blocks-ai-rivals-from-using-slack-data-according-to-reports", "label": "Reuters via Cyprus Mail, Salesforce blocks AI rivals from using Slack data, Jun 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$d7dd820d-e91f-5cc9-9668-a5f305400d3d$ml$::uuid, $ml$aa123d55-36fe-5ef1-b815-63992329275a$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In AI apps, power sits with whoever controls the data that fills the context window.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cyprus-mail.com/2025/06/13/salesforce-blocks-ai-rivals-from-using-slack-data-according-to-reports", "label": "Reuters via Cyprus Mail, Salesforce blocks AI rivals from using Slack data, Jun 2025"}, {"url": "https://anthropic.com/news/donating-the-model-context-protocol-and-establishing-of-the-agentic-ai-foundation", "label": "Anthropic, Donating MCP and the Agentic AI Foundation, Dec 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7b27437d-1b7d-51cb-aba9-7ff19ac37da6$ml$::uuid, $ml$0c614e20-fb67-56a7-827d-516ef2c28933$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 52 · The numbers$ml$, $ml$In 2024, NVIDIA researchers tested 17 models that claimed windows of 32,000 tokens or more. Only half held up at 32,000. The RULER benchmark asks models to find, trace and combine information hidden in long inputs, across 13 tasks. GPT-4 claimed 128,000 tokens, but its effective length, how far it read while still performing well, was 64,000. Its score fell from 96.6% at 4,000 tokens to 81.2% at 128,000. The gap between the claimed and the effective window is what to check before trusting a long input.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2404.06654v3", "label": "NVIDIA, RULER: What's the real context size of your long-context models?, 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$c13bb54e-5586-5451-a797-4b4ecac579c5$ml$::uuid, $ml$0c614e20-fb67-56a7-827d-516ef2c28933$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The metric$ml$, $ml$Effective context length is how far a model can read while still performing well. On RULER, GPT-4's was half of its claimed 128,000 tokens.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2404.06654v3", "label": "NVIDIA, RULER: What's the real context size of your long-context models?, 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$cbb619fc-c871-5fb6-9e6c-46f5d2bb8ab9$ml$::uuid, $ml$0c614e20-fb67-56a7-827d-516ef2c28933$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$Position matters$ml$, $ml$Models find facts best at the start or end of a long input. A 2023 study found accuracy drops when the key fact sits in the middle.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.03172v3", "label": "Liu et al., Lost in the Middle: how language models use long contexts, 2023"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$d1f7fffa-9270-5f4f-9164-2a5e7c66c623$ml$::uuid, $ml$0c614e20-fb67-56a7-827d-516ef2c28933$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$The number decides what you send$ml$, $ml$Past the effective length, more text can hurt. Teams trim inputs and put key facts first or last. The middle effect held even for models built for long inputs.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2404.06654v3", "label": "NVIDIA, RULER: What's the real context size of your long-context models?, 2024"}, {"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.03172v3", "label": "Liu et al., Lost in the Middle: how language models use long contexts, 2023"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$cab9ec1e-f9b2-5eec-865d-01d0b39d368a$ml$::uuid, $ml$0c614e20-fb67-56a7-827d-516ef2c28933$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Ask for the effective length$ml$, $ml$GPT-4 claimed 128,000 tokens but held up to 64,000 on RULER. Asking for the tested number marks you as careful.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2404.06654v3", "label": "NVIDIA, RULER: What's the real context size of your long-context models?, 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$9b1cc727-1e77-5f7d-a483-d9d48c8acad4$ml$::uuid, $ml$0c614e20-fb67-56a7-827d-516ef2c28933$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In long context, trust the effective length, not the advertised one.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2404.06654v3", "label": "NVIDIA, RULER: What's the real context size of your long-context models?, 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$cb9df644-b79e-5b1b-b036-f8d44f47a363$ml$::uuid, $ml$71b85fc7-6647-589b-804e-079cf9a086b4$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 52 · The numbers$ml$, $ml$In 2024, NVIDIA researchers tested 17 models that claimed windows of 32,000 tokens or more. Only half held up at 32,000. The RULER benchmark asks models to find, trace and combine information hidden in long inputs, across 13 tasks. GPT-4 claimed 128,000 tokens, but its effective length, how far it read while still performing well, was 64,000. Its score fell from 96.6% at 4,000 tokens to 81.2% at 128,000. The gap between the claimed and the effective window is what to check before trusting a long input.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2404.06654v3", "label": "NVIDIA, RULER: What's the real context size of your long-context models?, 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$83285af4-d284-5dae-939d-cd308a911954$ml$::uuid, $ml$71b85fc7-6647-589b-804e-079cf9a086b4$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The metric$ml$, $ml$Effective context length is how far a model can read while still performing well. On RULER, GPT-4's was half of its claimed 128,000 tokens.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2404.06654v3", "label": "NVIDIA, RULER: What's the real context size of your long-context models?, 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
