($ml$d4330c97-be21-57a2-8723-1bef8281f442$ml$::uuid, $ml$b12db8f6-fc4a-5e1d-a036-b5ec36b56fa9$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In AI apps, treat everything in the context window as untrusted, and limit what a fooled model can do.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.techradar.com/pro/security/prompt-injection-attacks-might-never-be-properly-mitigated-uk-ncsc-warns", "label": "TechRadar, UK NCSC warns prompt injection may never be fully mitigated, Dec 2025"}, {"url": "https://thehackernews.com/2025/06/zero-click-ai-vulnerability-exposes.html", "label": "The Hacker News, zero-click AI flaw in Microsoft 365 Copilot, Jun 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$53afa357-bddc-5f3e-b60c-f781fec2f440$ml$::uuid, $ml$856c202a-c26b-5227-9b6d-cde5b0511e71$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 54 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In 2025, a Microsoft survey of 31,000 workers in 31 countries ranked prompt engineer second from the bottom of new roles companies planned to add. Two years earlier, prompt engineers had been among the hottest hires in AI, with salaries of up to $200,000. The survey put AI coding, AI data interpretation and AI security at the top instead. The work did not vanish. In September 2025, Anthropic described context engineering, curating everything a model sees, as the natural progression of prompt engineering.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.kornferry.com/insights/this-week-in-leadership/the-hottest-job-of-the-year-goes-cold", "label": "Korn Ferry, The hottest job of the year goes cold, Apr 2025"}, {"url": "https://anthropic.com/research/effective-context-engineering-for-ai-agents", "label": "Anthropic, Effective context engineering for AI agents, Sep 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b19e715a-28ad-56ce-8d1c-21dade019256$ml$::uuid, $ml$856c202a-c26b-5227-9b6d-cde5b0511e71$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The new name$ml$, $ml$Context engineering is finding the smallest set of high-signal tokens for a model to see. Anthropic calls it the natural progression of prompt engineering.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://anthropic.com/research/effective-context-engineering-for-ai-agents", "label": "Anthropic, Effective context engineering for AI agents, Sep 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$0004c94b-aa15-554b-90f2-9b510a865f59$ml$::uuid, $ml$856c202a-c26b-5227-9b6d-cde5b0511e71$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$Longer inputs make models less reliable, even on simple tasks. Chroma tested 18 models in July 2025 and named the effect context rot.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://trychroma.com/research/context-rot", "label": "Chroma, Context Rot technical report, Jul 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$65b2b920-d2f8-5143-b3d2-01c3b68eee8a$ml$::uuid, $ml$856c202a-c26b-5227-9b6d-cde5b0511e71$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Agents now manage their own context$ml$, $ml$They summarize old turns, keep notes outside the window and hand side tasks to sub-agents. Each keeps the window lean. Sub-agents return short summaries instead of all their work.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://anthropic.com/research/effective-context-engineering-for-ai-agents", "label": "Anthropic, Effective context engineering for AI agents, Sep 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
