($ml$96dc331f-75cc-5e6c-a863-299e3b1ff6d9$ml$::uuid, $ml$de8bf8fc-f064-5e13-865a-9ada05e7fc53$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In AI, open weights let you run a model; open source lets you rebuild it.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://siliconangle.com/2024/10/28/osi-clarifies-makes-ai-systems-open-source-open-models-fall-short/", "label": "SiliconANGLE, OSI defines open source AI and open models fall short, Oct 2024"}, {"url": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-oss/", "label": "OpenAI, Introducing gpt-oss, Aug 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$0bf857a0-f243-5d40-9b75-02653c1a6261$ml$::uuid, $ml$bc71fa99-2854-5380-8424-a4f13d291a84$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 56 · The money$ml$, $ml$Mistral gives away many of its models. Its annual revenue run rate still went from $20 million to over $400 million in a year. Mistral's CEO Arthur Mensch told the Financial Times in February 2026 that its annualized run rate was north of $400 million, up from $20 million a year earlier. The Paris company was founded in 2023 and publishes models anyone can download. Its paying customers include ASML, TotalEnergies and HSBC.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.hl.co.uk/shares/stock-market-news/company--news/mistral-invests-in-swedish-infrastructure-as-annual-revenues-top-$400m", "label": "Sharecast via Hargreaves Lansdown, Mistral revenues top $400m, Feb 2026"}, {"url": "https://startupfortune.com/mistral-ai-at-20-billion-is-a-bet-on-european-sovereign-ai-coming-into-its-own/", "label": "Startup Fortune, Mistral AI at 20 billion, Jun 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$488bb22e-120c-55c7-b566-77eabfa0cd3a$ml$::uuid, $ml$bc71fa99-2854-5380-8424-a4f13d291a84$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The giveaway$ml$, $ml$In December 2025, Mistral released all its Mistral 3 models under the Apache 2.0 license. Mistral Large 3 has 675 billion parameters and trained on 3,000 NVIDIA H200 GPUs.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://mistral.ai/news/mistral-3", "label": "Mistral AI, Introducing Mistral 3, Dec 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$f5612ee6-681c-5296-a4bf-98234c976de1$ml$::uuid, $ml$bc71fa99-2854-5380-8424-a4f13d291a84$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$Another motive$ml$, $ml$Meta gives Llama away for a different reason. Zuckerberg wrote in 2024 that selling access to AI models isn't Meta's business model. He wanted to avoid being locked into a competitor's closed ecosystem.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://about.fb.com/news/2024/07/open-source-ai-is-the-path-forward/", "label": "Mark Zuckerberg, Open Source AI Is the Path Forward, Jul 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$13b3bff1-4783-5510-bfbb-fa4fff2fa613$ml$::uuid, $ml$bc71fa99-2854-5380-8424-a4f13d291a84$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Open models push prices down$ml$, $ml$In April 2026, Artificial Analysis found top open models matched leading closed ones closely. They cost half to one sixth as much. Zuckerberg claimed Llama 3.1 405B could run at about half the cost of GPT-4o.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://artificialanalysis.ai/articles/recent-open-weights-model-launches", "label": "Artificial Analysis, recent open weights model launches, Apr 2026"}, {"url": "https://about.fb.com/news/2024/07/open-source-ai-is-the-path-forward/", "label": "Mark Zuckerberg, Open Source AI Is the Path Forward, Jul 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
