($ml$75952018-70aa-56c8-a813-ddcb55c207e6$ml$::uuid, $ml$f4683fd5-826f-5f50-88f4-3640d29e4f21$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$The US wants its own open leaders$ml$, $ml$In July 2025, the White House AI Action Plan called for leading American open models. Meta still launched Muse Spark closed. The plan says the choice to release open or closed is up to the developer.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://fedscoop.com/open-source-ai-trump-ai-action-plan/", "label": "FedScoop, open source in the AI Action Plan, Jul 2025"}, {"url": "https://www.artificialintelligence-news.com/news/meta-muse-spark-ai-model-open-source/", "label": "AI News, Meta launches Muse Spark as a proprietary model, Apr 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$511aed8a-32aa-59f6-a0fc-e3d6aa99897a$ml$::uuid, $ml$f4683fd5-826f-5f50-88f4-3640d29e4f21$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Free models spread influence$ml$, $ml$The US AI Action Plan says open models could become global standards, which gives them geostrategic value.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://fedscoop.com/open-source-ai-trump-ai-action-plan/", "label": "FedScoop, open source in the AI Action Plan, Jul 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$913c26b7-aa1c-510a-b6e8-e441302ac567$ml$::uuid, $ml$f4683fd5-826f-5f50-88f4-3640d29e4f21$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In open AI, power goes to whoever everyone else builds on.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://huggingface.co/blog/huggingface/state-of-os-hf-spring-2026", "label": "Hugging Face, State of Open Source on Hugging Face: Spring 2026"}, {"url": "https://hai.stanford.edu/assets/files/hai-digichina-issue-brief-beyond-deepseek-chinas-diverse-open-weight-ai-ecosystem-policy-implications.pdf", "label": "Stanford HAI and DigiChina, Beyond DeepSeek: China's open-weight AI ecosystem, Dec 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$5b5ed71a-3567-52ab-ac02-3c9c402973a8$ml$::uuid, $ml$3c6ed8e1-b600-56b8-a917-1d1ed17e5bda$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 58 · The numbers$ml$, $ml$In May 2023, the best closed model beat the best open one by 15.2% on a chat leaderboard. By August 2024 the gap was 0.5%. Stanford's 2026 AI Index tracks the top open-weight and closed models on the Arena Leaderboard, where people vote between answers. GPT-4 led Vicuna-13B by 174 points in May 2023. Releases like Llama 3.1 405B cut the gap to 7 points by August 2024. Then new closed models pulled ahead: by March 2026 the gap was 49 points, or 3.4%.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://hai.stanford.edu/assets/files/ai_index_report_2026_chapter_2_technical.pdf", "label": "Stanford AI Index 2026, chapter 2, technical performance"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$3fc19158-69ac-5095-8a6c-1cc15e155ae5$ml$::uuid, $ml$3c6ed8e1-b600-56b8-a917-1d1ed17e5bda$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$Today$ml$, $ml$In March 2026 the top closed model led the top open one, GLM-5, by 49 points. Six of the top ten models on the leaderboard were closed.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://hai.stanford.edu/assets/files/ai_index_report_2026_chapter_2_technical.pdf", "label": "Stanford AI Index 2026, chapter 2, technical performance"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$5cbb8faf-48d0-5a8f-985f-01d180996fee$ml$::uuid, $ml$3c6ed8e1-b600-56b8-a917-1d1ed17e5bda$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$In months$ml$, $ml$Epoch AI measures the gap in time. Since January 2026, open models have trailed the best closed ones by about four months. That equals about 8 points on its capability index.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://epoch.ai/data-insights/open-closed-eci-gap", "label": "Epoch AI, the open and closed capability gap, May 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$1ab72248-b7ca-5d12-8236-56755955a459$ml$::uuid, $ml$3c6ed8e1-b600-56b8-a917-1d1ed17e5bda$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Each big closed release reopens the gap$ml$, $ml$Open models catch up, then a new closed model jumps ahead. The AI Index describes open systems closing in, then falling behind. DeepSeek-R1 once trailed OpenAI's o1 by just 5 points.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://hai.stanford.edu/assets/files/ai_index_report_2026_chapter_2_technical.pdf", "label": "Stanford AI Index 2026, chapter 2, technical performance"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$d1244af2-1098-5294-9ba6-5163ddeb80ca$ml$::uuid, $ml$3c6ed8e1-b600-56b8-a917-1d1ed17e5bda$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Quote the gap with its date$ml$, $ml$Say the open gap was 0.5% in August 2024 and 3.4% in March 2026. A gap figure without a date misleads.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://hai.stanford.edu/assets/files/ai_index_report_2026_chapter_2_technical.pdf", "label": "Stanford AI Index 2026, chapter 2, technical performance"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$951e1f17-0a48-5a41-b7d1-a551d243024b$ml$::uuid, $ml$3c6ed8e1-b600-56b8-a917-1d1ed17e5bda$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In AI, the open gap is measured in months, and it resets with each closed release.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://epoch.ai/data-insights/open-closed-eci-gap", "label": "Epoch AI, the open and closed capability gap, May 2026"}, {"url": "https://hai.stanford.edu/assets/files/ai_index_report_2026_chapter_2_technical.pdf", "label": "Stanford AI Index 2026, chapter 2, technical performance"}]$ml$::jsonb),
