($ml$ed1dc057-a4b2-5060-bf63-c70e0bf171c9$ml$::uuid, $ml$582f4b72-f3df-535b-b4a3-0bb73d091f17$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$Standard licenses$ml$, $ml$Many Chinese labs use standard licenses instead. Qwen3 ships under Apache 2.0 and DeepSeek-R1 under MIT. Moonshot's Kimi K2 uses a modified MIT license asking big commercial users for credit.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://hai.stanford.edu/assets/files/hai-digichina-issue-brief-beyond-deepseek-chinas-diverse-open-weight-ai-ecosystem-policy-implications.pdf", "label": "Stanford HAI and DigiChina, Beyond DeepSeek: China's open-weight AI ecosystem, Dec 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$28d680ba-b6e5-5d88-bbb8-d9ef8ea089e5$ml$::uuid, $ml$582f4b72-f3df-535b-b4a3-0bb73d091f17$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$EU law gives open models a partial pass$ml$, $ml$Under the EU AI Act, free and open-source models can skip some documentation duties. Models with systemic risk get no such pass. Training with more than 10^25 FLOP makes a model presumed to carry systemic risk. Open models must still publish a summary of their training data.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/guidelines-obligations-gpai-providers", "label": "European Commission, FAQ on obligations for general-purpose AI providers"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$54ec3e28-779a-514d-80eb-38bc9de37f71$ml$::uuid, $ml$582f4b72-f3df-535b-b4a3-0bb73d091f17$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$License terms shape the market$ml$, $ml$A license that excludes EU firms or the largest companies shrinks who can sell products built on it.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2025/04/05/meta-releases-llama-4-a-new-crop-of-flagship-ai-models", "label": "TechCrunch, Meta releases Llama 4, Apr 2025"}, {"url": "https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-4-Maverick-17B-128E-Original", "label": "Meta, Llama 4 Maverick model card and license"}]$ml$::jsonb),
